	file.0000000000000001.title: "&6&lCosmic Frontiers"
	quest.00557FB9FEF4A039.quest_desc: [
		"Factory Gauges allow you to create stockpile requests for various materials."
		""
		"This could help you early on when it comes to routing items and fluid."
	]
	quest.00557FB9FEF4A039.quest_subtitle: "Simple Stockpile Automation"
	quest.008703F2EB317107.quest_desc: [
		"Many sources of Silicon and other materials require access to an MV electrolyzer."
		""
		""
		"Silicon, just like Aluminium, has a few recipes available at LV tier, but it is STRONGLY RECOMMENDED to upgrade your electrolyzer firstly!"
	]
	quest.008703F2EB317107.quest_subtitle: "The Products for Boules"
	quest.008703F2EB317107.title: "Boule Prepwork"
	quest.00E576A121E8BDF8.quest_desc: [
		"Knives can be used on tall grass to occasionally get straw alongside seeds."
		""
		"This could be useful for making your packed mud, if you're struggling to farm it."
	]
	quest.00E576A121E8BDF8.quest_subtitle: "A solution!"
	quest.00E576A121E8BDF8.title: "Straw Problems?"
	quest.011BFFD7A89C98EE.quest_desc: [
		"You may have noticed your distillation towers can swap modes to vac distillation."
		""
		"This is where the configuration itself is used. You'll need to attach an aluminium vacuum module to your DT"
	]
	quest.011BFFD7A89C98EE.quest_subtitle: "Mode Switching Time!"
	quest.011BFFD7A89C98EE.title: "About your DT"
	quest.02049F5FDD7273A7.quest_desc: [
		"Less annoyances in terms of source oil production."
		""
		""
		"However, *why*, i mean i guess it's not bad, 960EU/mb is extremely strong for an LV fuel."
		""
		"Just uh, seed and fish oil are rather annoying to get at scale, keep that in mind."
	]
	quest.02049F5FDD7273A7.quest_subtitle: "Just... go make source diesel."
	quest.027BFC59C42DA1AC.quest_desc: [
		"1k storages allow you to do one thing early on other storage sizes done, spam out a bunch of drives for types. "
		""
		"It is common when first building your AE2 network you will always have more item types than item volume, 1k storage cells are perfect for soaking this type-bloat cost."
		""
		"Once you got the majority of random junk in your system, you can make bigger drives to fill them with your bulk materials/resources."
	]
	quest.027BFC59C42DA1AC.quest_subtitle: "Early digital storage"
	quest.028BF3C5997A6B13.quest_subtitle: "Option 2: Frimament"
	quest.02DDCF50B2E0BF28.quest_desc: [
		"This allows you to recover sodium hydroxide and silicon dioxide, both things you used to produce your bauxite slurry earlier."
		""
		""
		"It is recommended to recycle this to avoid wasting all your sodium hydroxide"
	]
	quest.02DDCF50B2E0BF28.quest_subtitle: "Get your sodium hydroxide back"
	quest.0327682C5CD80700.quest_subtitle: "Smells..."
	quest.0404FA9ACCD11D51.quest_desc: [
		"You can make Hulls and Casings Cheaper with a small cost of Rubber or Plastics."
		""
		"Notably, check out the MV Hull shortcut recipe, as well as previous tiers."
	]
	quest.0404FA9ACCD11D51.quest_subtitle: "Cheaper Hulls and Casings"
	quest.0404FA9ACCD11D51.title: "Got some Rubbers and Plastics?"
	quest.0407A0291D69959D.quest_subtitle: "You could cause a produce shortage with this..."
	quest.04D15703B3D383E2.quest_desc: [
		"You may have noticed you produce a large amount of chunks, which need to be crushed into powders to be used further."
		""
		"Macerators are useful for this task, but are also slow and offer no parallel beyond the early game steam grinder. Asking players to make quads of these or use a steam-tier machine in a scaled ore sorter setup sounded absurd, so the result is the powderizer can also macerate only ore chunks."
		""
		"Powderizers spend more EU than macerators to shred chunks into dusts. But also gains the 8 Pure Parallels of the powderizer (eg. spending only 1 recipes worth of eu on 8 recipes)"
		""
		"Powderizers are arguably more expensive than a steam grinder, but offer more flexibility overall and are faster."
	]
	quest.04D15703B3D383E2.quest_subtitle: "A better industrial macerator"
	quest.04D15703B3D383E2.title: "Powderizer Secondary Uses"
	quest.04E6BCCDEBBE8555.quest_desc: [
		"Uh, it makes 1920eu/t"
		""
		"This puts it at a fuel density nearly as strong as HV's Cetane Boosted Diesel."
		""
		"I will, probably have to nerf this. "
		""
		"*edits scripts*"
		""
		"Okay, you probably see it as 640eu/t Still rather strong for an LV fuel, but uh..."
		""
		"Lord have mercy sometimes I'm horrible at balancing lol."
		""
		""
		"Anyway, this requires a lot of extra setup for the yield it gives, it does however grant Glycerol, useful for early chemistry if electrolyzed into hydrogen and oxygen and carbon."
	]
	quest.04E6BCCDEBBE8555.quest_subtitle: "Possibly Overtuned"
	quest.0584A322CC8C1A28.quest_desc: [
		"Sable and Create Aeronautics allow for creation of contraptions with real time simulated physics."
		"These contraptions are amazing for creating flying ships/cars/drills"
		""
		"Please take caution using them, make constant backups, with a phyiscs mod like this even though it is almost perfect, it still will have edgecase issues we'll most likely find."
	]
	quest.0584A322CC8C1A28.quest_subtitle: "Redefining the game."
	quest.05D76DF50301384D.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to your first(?) significant chemical setup, &bChromium&r."
		""
		"This chain aims to teach you basic automation skills like recycling and looping intermediate products. While also being one of the few things seperating you from AE2. "
		""
		""
		"&o&7This dust seems to have a much more valuable material trapped inside it, I should process this.&r"
	]
	quest.05D76DF50301384D.quest_subtitle: "The Start"
	quest.068F151533C124CD.quest_desc: [
		"Applied Energistics 2 is your mainstay source of fluid and item logistics from here on out."
		""
		""
		"While you've had access to create logistics for automatic setups. It is time to start to consider AE2 as the objective upgrade. "
		""
		""
		"AE2 is not only stronger throughput wise, but offers a lot more flexibility and throughput which is vital for GT setups to function without stalling or delay."
		""
		""
		"AE2 also has a host of addons to assist in building your base."
		""
		"&6"
		"&6NOTICE : AE2 in Frontiers has multiple custom mechanics that heavily alter AE2 gameplay, &6guides may not help as much with some systems. Please report all bugs directly to the &6Fronteirs repo, rather than AE2, Firstly.&r"
		""
		"&cNo like seriously, AE2 is drastically changed, do not report bugs to mod authors!"
	]
	quest.068F151533C124CD.quest_subtitle: "The Titan of the Digital Age"
	quest.072350DCC099E9C9.quest_desc: [
		"Using a flocculant you can help seperate materials further. The resulting ore yields have more unique products and a slight material yield bonus. "
		""
		"Flocculant solution (Polyethylene Oxide) rates have been mostly made on guesswork of how bad it'd be. I was going to do 25mb per but it felt pretty unforgiving. 10mb seems the best option but if we need to nudge it around to 5mb or 15mb I am not opposed to it. Let me know your feedback on Github or Discord."
	]
	quest.072350DCC099E9C9.quest_subtitle: "Flocculation (Tier 3 Ore Processing)"
	quest.073308BA37C957AF.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to the real deal, Autocrafting!"
		""
		"Autocrafting allows you to send materials directly to machines from your terminal, and even chain steps together."
		""
		"Just make sure your AE2 grid has enough spare CWU for the craft, as crafts consume CWU and Bytes the larger they get."
		""
		"If you haven't been keeping your system supplied with CWU properly yet, now you'll have to as crafts can not be started with a CWU overload, and providers will stop if CWU overloads during an active craft."
	]
	quest.073308BA37C957AF.quest_subtitle: "The King of Autocrafting"
	quest.07A3009B253FF22E.quest_desc: [
		"These flames cause cannon peppers to rapidly mutate into a pile of overloaded sacs."
		""
		"These overloaded pearls seem to stabilize into a mechanical biosystem, they most likely will be suitable to hold these memory fragments you've produced."
		""
		""
		"Let's try creating a core that can handle all of these mildly delicate materials."
	]
	quest.07A3009B253FF22E.quest_subtitle: "Nature of the nether gone wild"
	quest.07D19BDB1D7C756D.quest_desc: ["to be able to sort your ores into more useful products, the crushed ore mush first be washed and seperated in a flotation plant"]
	quest.07D19BDB1D7C756D.quest_subtitle: "Washing your ores (Tier 1 Ore Processing)"
	quest.084D9D116B8A6C4A.quest_subtitle: "Biological Scrap Metals"
	quest.09051494F3867278.quest_desc: [
		"You had to (most likely) make one of these for PTFE."
		""
		"If you haven't probably go do that first, lol"
	]
	quest.09051494F3867278.quest_subtitle: "You should be familiar with this one"
	quest.095B0A02540AE6B1.quest_subtitle: "The Primary Ore Source (in HV)"
	quest.09743DE5EC36B7A3.quest_desc: [
		"To Reach the Firmament you must use the \"&eAscension to the Firmament&r\" Ritual (Check for it in EMI!)"
		""
		"The Ritual Type it uses is called &bFatma's Incentivized Attraction&r and requires the following chalks"
		""
		"- Black (LV)"
		"- White (Steam)"
		"- Lime (Steam)"
		"- Red (LV)"
		"- Orange (LV)"
		"- Blue (MV)"
		""
		"Upon ritual activation and subsequent, players will be sent upwards to the firmament."
		"You can leave the firmament by jumping into the ammonia sea below and holding shift."
		""
		"It is recommended to bring some kind of teleporter with you so you can get back easier than using a ritual every time."
		""
		"&6Ritual must be able to see the sky&r"
	]
	quest.09743DE5EC36B7A3.title: "How to reach the Firmament"
	quest.0975CA11110DC9FB.quest_desc: [
		"Kanthal and Silicon require being cooled down with water before use."
		""
		"If you haven't already while your kanthal smelts, make a chemical bath and get the hot ingots cooling as they exit your EBFs."
	]
	quest.0975CA11110DC9FB.quest_subtitle: "You probably want a chemical bath too..."
	quest.0A5E16599EAFAEC6.quest_desc: [
		"Terminals allow you to access your linked storage inside of AE2."
		""
		"Terminals will natively display all available fluids and items, which you can extract/insert from the terminal itself."
		""
		"Terminals take up 1 channel per terminal."
	]
	quest.0A5E16599EAFAEC6.quest_subtitle: "Seeing into AE2"
	quest.0AB55A192BC06F35.quest_subtitle: "Late SMD Components"
	quest.0B34B5CE7CCBAE72.quest_desc: [
		"Note : GT Miners do not work in the Undergarden or Abyss."
		""
		"Mining Ores in the Abyss will require specalized infrastructure at a later date, but most products you need to progress are automation chains once you've collected a initial bounty from a specific layer."
	]
	quest.0B34B5CE7CCBAE72.title: "Why isn't my miner working?"
	quest.0BFB4FBAD5FE77F1.quest_desc: [
		"Okay, to give you a breakdown of the power changes within this pack. It's easy to bullet them out and then explain each."
		""
		""
		"1. Cable loss removal"
		"2. Increased amperage capacity"
		"3. Multiamp power consumption"
		""
		""
		"Most recipes take anywhere from 1-4 Amps, with some even exceeding this into 6-16 Amps (For extremely powerful machines). This means to start LV, you most likely want 4 Steam Turbines."
		""
		"All wires and cables have had cable loss removed, effectively acting like classic GT Superconductors."
		""
		"The difference here is, cables that were low loss or lossless now boast huge Amperage limits."
		"Wires still will damage mobs and players if not made into a cable, Superconductor class wires do not."
		""
		"In short, you'll be making a lot, and i mean A LOT, more power. Part of the challenge will be managing your wire networks to avoid over-amperage."
	]
	quest.0BFB4FBAD5FE77F1.quest_subtitle: "A bit of reading before we start."
	quest.0BFB4FBAD5FE77F1.title: "A Crashcourse on the new power systems"
	quest.0C0E3F2E637DA0A9.quest_desc: [
		"You've been able to alloy smelt dawnstone, but you need some in molten form to create aspecti."
		""
		""
		"Use a melter powered with a small amount of ember to makee your first molten dawnstone."
	]
	quest.0C0E3F2E637DA0A9.quest_subtitle: "Dawnstone but Molten"
	quest.0C2BE4EC08B241F1.quest_desc: [
		"This is the start of Platinum Seperation."
		""
		"The primary yields are mostly Platinum and Palladium, and a strange insoluable powder you will use later."
		""
		"Do note, until you can do the full Platinum processing chain, this process is lossy on chemical feedstocks like Chlorine, Hydrogen, Oxygen, and Nitrogen. "
		""
		"I would strongly recommend setting up mass automation for Acids, Ammonia, and other various common chemicals before tackling this. "
		""
		""
		"Many things within this chain can also be recycled and metered with enough finnesse on a AE2 Subnet. There's plenty of ways to tackle this, so I wish you luck!"
	]
	quest.0C2BE4EC08B241F1.quest_subtitle: "The 'efficient' way"
	quest.0C77536FF23F6946.quest_desc: [
		"Made with that yellow dust you got from the nether, Sulfuric, and a pile of basic elements like hydrogen and oxygen (or water in some cases)"
		""
		""
		"There's several methods you can take to reach Sulfuric Acid, I will let you decide which works for you."
		""
		""
		"Also worth noting, you will need a gold drum or pipes to safely move sulfuric acid around!"
	]
	quest.0C77536FF23F6946.quest_subtitle: "The other orange fluid, besides Ethanol"
	quest.0DC63A0B32F403DE.quest_desc: [
		"Unfortunately, unlike MV where you could quickly get access to the tiers energy hatch, this one is a little (see: a LOT) more involved."
		""
		"You'll need to make a cleanroom, a multiblock which requires multiple polymers, concrete, and plenty of metals to assemble. Notably, &ePolytetrafluoroethylene&r is required, and &eMethane&r is only produced via &aWood Gas phase seperation&r at these early stages. "
		""
		""
		"In short, your first goal is to look southward of this quest on how to get PTFE and Methane."
		"Some of these machines are quite large, and may get cramped inside of buildings unless you build ahead. Don't forget, rain sealant spraycans exist!"
		""
		"Dev note: I built part of my petrochemical refinement stuff outdoors, which is what gave me this idea. "
	]
	quest.0DC63A0B32F403DE.quest_subtitle: "Uh Oh! Surprise!"
	quest.0DE75C5D598B331B.quest_desc: [
		"Distill Wood Vinegar again to get Spirits and Liqour"
		""
		"Both of those can then be distilled once again into their final products."
		""
		"I trust you can use EMI by now to see those products, if you somehow made it here without EMI..."
		"How? Better yet, why?"
	]
	quest.0DE75C5D598B331B.quest_subtitle: "Double Distillation Trouble"
	quest.0E46D7EB999D3897.quest_subtitle: "The easy part"
	quest.0EC4D52E2252406D.quest_subtitle: "Hey, these are modules by the way!"
	quest.0EC5D1285DF63FF4.quest_desc: [
		"Steam Components are rather useful for logistics early on, allowing you a source of extraction/insertion for items and fluids."
		""
		""
		"While not strictly required to craft any machines (still undecided on that), the early game logistics and reduced cost compared to constantly using LV conveyors/pumps is much easier."
	]
	quest.0EC5D1285DF63FF4.quest_subtitle: "Steam Parts"
	quest.0F51CE9E96545226.quest_desc: [
		"Vac Residuals lead you towards multiple different routes of processing. It is up to you to decide what suits your base"
		""
		""
		"Notable options would be to phase seperate it and recycle the outputs"
		""
		"You could optionally convert it towards syngas and produce a metric amount of hydrogen."
		""
		"This also loops back out towards general out products again, so hopefully by now you've gotten the hang of this"
	]
	quest.0F51CE9E96545226.quest_subtitle: "Scary"
	quest.0FA8D92F9734C77C.quest_subtitle: "The Sulfur Ore Field"
	quest.0FDE4203D468D05F.quest_desc: [
		"Soul Resin is extracted from Soul gourds, however you do not have the extraction tools needed to do this quite yet."
		""
		"So for now, craft and fuel an Embers &bMelter&r to melt the entire gourd for some resin."
		""
		""
		"Once you reach the LV tier, you can use a normal extractor to get the fluid out of these gourds easily."
	]
	quest.0FDE4203D468D05F.quest_subtitle: "Solidified Pumpkins?"
	quest.1109F476F38A663D.quest_desc: ["Required to make HV Hulls"]
	quest.1109F476F38A663D.quest_subtitle: "You'll need this"
	quest.113BA0DDF76D33E3.quest_desc: [
		"Cladding allows the components inside of your machine casings to stay functional even in the worst conditions."
		""
		"Now, that doesn't make them water proof, let alone safe to keep outside"
		""
		"&c&lRemember! Machines exposed to rain OR fluid will catch fire and attempt to explode, be careful!"
	]
	quest.113BA0DDF76D33E3.quest_subtitle: "Shielding"
	quest.1198F042E7F71D7F.quest_subtitle: "FUTURE CONTENT: 0.9.0+"
	quest.11A80F269275F15D.quest_desc: [
		"The deeper you decend, the more agressive murkbloom seems to become."
		""
		"Your earlier stealth fiber won't keep you hidden as effectively so it is time for an upgrade!"
	]
	quest.11A80F269275F15D.quest_subtitle: "Not really a suggestion"
	quest.12BEB88ECEFDBBBA.quest_desc: ["Compute Cores convert energy into CWU for your network components to run."]
	quest.12BEB88ECEFDBBBA.quest_subtitle: "Adding CWU to AE"
	quest.12D1C8CC27AE39B2.quest_desc: [
		"Pattern Buffers basically act like a Pattern Provider, with some extra QOL quirks to make machine crafting easier."
		""
		"1. Each pattern in an ME Buffer has it's own isolated inventory for fluids/items, meaning &apatterns can not conflict&r."
		"1.1 However, this means patterns must contain all ingredients, shared resources (like EBF gasses) included!"
		"1.2 There are \"shared\" inventory slots inside of each ME Buffer, this can hold items like non-consumable catalysts/molds"
		""
		"2. Pattern proxies are bound to pattern buffers with data sticks, shift right click your pattern buffer, and then right click a proxy. Proxies mirror the contents of a pattern buffer, making automation arrays for crafts easier."
		""
		"3. Pattern Buffers also can store a quite frankly titanic amount of internal storage, this means machines will run at their full force when possible. This matters greatly when you have mechanics that rely on it, such as parallel."
		""
		"4. Buffers are exposed like normal to AE2 pattern terminals, meaning you can access your patterns as normal."
	]
	quest.12D1C8CC27AE39B2.quest_subtitle: "The King and Queen of Autocrafting"
	quest.130F6EE5889B7ADE.quest_desc: [
		"Cart Assemblers are quite frankly way too strong."
		""
		"However, for now they will remain teired here, if they need to be uptiered then we'll handle it then."
	]
	quest.130F6EE5889B7ADE.quest_subtitle: "Pretty Defined"
	quest.14B068EF3C3192DB.quest_desc: [
		"Stormglass seems like an unrefined crystal useful in making weather resistant glassware"
		""
		"There's a bounty of other materials in the Firmament, I've gathered what I can for now..."
		""
		""
		"Many of the basic blocks in the firmament have a use at establishing yourself in the Firmament, look through EMI to figure out a path forward along with future quests!"
	]
	quest.14B068EF3C3192DB.quest_subtitle: "New Materials to Exploit"
	quest.14B068EF3C3192DB.title: "Firmament Geology"
	quest.14D6F3083E2DD469.quest_desc: [
		"This pressure module will allow you to survive deeper in the Hollowed Abyss "
		"up to -600m"
	]
	quest.14D6F3083E2DD469.quest_subtitle: "Tier Three Armor"
	quest.15DCE4A5DE87DF3A.quest_subtitle: "To the souls who were never found"
	quest.15DCE4A5DE87DF3A.title: "The Bottom of the Abyss?"
	quest.15E83FF40983A8F5.quest_desc: [
		"Allows you to carry a little extra 'stuff' (abstract) on your player."
		""
		"Useful when going mining to carry more ores home :)"
	]
	quest.15E83FF40983A8F5.quest_subtitle: "Backpacks"
	quest.15F0753A300EE4E9.quest_desc: [
		"allows you to expose items/fluids to machines for crafting. Useful for passive multiblocks or specialized crafting setups."
		""
		""
		"NOTE: These blocks are currently being Optimized on GTM's side, we've applied the patch to the pack to test it."
		"If you notice your base starts to lag with many of these, please provide us a spark profile so we can look into it farther."
		""
		"In general, you should be able to freely use this without much issue, but please keep in mind these may show up on Observable/Spark readouts if you use thousands and thousands of them"
	]
	quest.15F0753A300EE4E9.quest_subtitle: "Stocking what's needed"
	quest.16207443D5974CEA.quest_desc: [
		"Yippie! You got Titanium!"
		""
		""
		"To actually make this, if you're confused, you will need Nichrome Coils to produce the heat needed to smelt the Titanium Tetrachloride into ingots."
		""
		""
		"The Magnesium is fully looped, btw, so you might want a dedicated set of EBFS and machines to let this passive run"
	]
	quest.16207443D5974CEA.quest_subtitle: "Titanium : Goal!"
	quest.168A6B3A2FD0CC45.quest_subtitle: "For the simple machines"
	quest.168A6B3A2FD0CC45.title: "Basic LV Parts"
	quest.16B7E08679F3FA97.quest_desc: [
		"This multi is your pathway forwards to permanent power infrastructure."
		""
		"Each MPS can be built at dynamic lengths to generate anywhere from 16 to 64 Amps of power."
		""
		"The stator coils used inside of the MPS will determine what hatch you may place as an output."
		""
		"And the type of internal component you use will determine if the MPS uses steam/gas fuels or liquid combustion fuels."
		""
		""
		"EMI and terminal in-wold preview can be configured to the length you desire."
		""
		"For further information/visualization, check out the ponder as well as read various tooltips."
		""
		"The MPS can also be throttled within the multiblocks menu, reducing production but also reducing fuel consumption"
		""
		"I apologize how difficult this structure is to build at the moment due to Terminal still being a WIP for GTM V8"
	]
	quest.16B7E08679F3FA97.quest_subtitle: "The Modular Power Station"
	quest.16B7E08679F3FA97.title: "The Most Important Power Multiblock"
	quest.16EE5D3DB14F4331.quest_desc: [
		""
		"          &l&f Craft a Nether permit, unlocking nether Access."
		""
		""
		""
		" &7In a unknown world far from here"
		" &7Sits a titan made of brass and gears"
		" &7Far beyond the nebulae and the stars "
		" &7She gleams into a world of her own design"
		" &7She painted the skies how she loved them"
		" &7And gave the grass the scent she remembers"
		" &7All for a love that will never be recieved the way she percieved"
		""
		" &7She watches, in curiousity, as you assemble a monolith of obsidian"
		" &7and strike it with fire."
		""
		" &o\"&aImpressive, dimensional awareness&r\"&r, &7She utters, with interest piqued."
		""
		"&7You march onward, into the mouth of hell; unaware of who observes you."
	]
	quest.16EE5D3DB14F4331.quest_subtitle: "Granting Access to Hell"
	quest.18153CD2A0487F03.quest_desc: ["Spirit Fire can be created by throwing a demons dream fruit on the ground, and lighting it on fire."]
	quest.18153CD2A0487F03.quest_subtitle: "Calm Flames"
	quest.184972E80D9D1F2C.quest_desc: [
		"Gonna be honest Its like, basically just like the malum spirit altar but with more whacky placement restrictions"
		""
		"The worn notebook has more info on it, if that's for some reason needed."
		""
		"If i'm being for real, might just make this a multi, cause idk if this thing still obliterates FPS or not..."
	]
	quest.184972E80D9D1F2C.quest_subtitle: "This uh, thing."
	quest.18E0AFF44EE3DEEC.quest_desc: [
		"One early way of getting oxygen is from centrifuging air."
		""
		"It's generally lower power draw than other methods make it a nice starting source for both nitrogen and oxygen."
	]
	quest.18E0AFF44EE3DEEC.quest_subtitle: "Air Centrifuging and Others"
	quest.194C6A5A0002FF5C.quest_subtitle: "Cool flames to temper"
	quest.1A6796453259700D.quest_desc: [
		"Storage busses are one of the few blocks from AE2 you will become very familiar with by the end of this game. Storage busses as their name implies will expose any storage they're attached to to the ME network."
		""
		"This is immediately useful for when you have large item storages, like silos or vaults, and want to interface them with AE2."
		""
		"Storage busses can also push items, this is useful on subnets notably with the setup below"
		""
		"Item output -- into an interface -> on a subnet with a storage bus -> storage bus pushes the contents to your main network."
		""
		""
		"This allows you to make very high throughput item movement with simple parts. Subnets as a whole will most likely have their own quest as well, but this is an extra tip. "
	]
	quest.1A6796453259700D.quest_subtitle: "A whole world of possibilities"
	quest.1AB5A5EFAE74D076.quest_subtitle: "The minimum."
	quest.1ADD84CA84189352.quest_desc: [
		"You'll need at least the following of these machines"
		""
		"- Pyrolyse Oven"
		"- Phase Separator"
		"- Fractional Condensor"
	]
	quest.1ADD84CA84189352.quest_subtitle: "Getting prepared for wood processing"
	quest.1B15278C77223BF4.quest_subtitle: "Turning Essentia Vitae into Anima"
	quest.1B387FD15E883317.quest_desc: [
		"You'll need materials, lots of them, and that starts with *you* extracting them."
		""
		""
		""
		"Work with me here, and I'll lead you towards a legendary tool, otherwise, make your own."
	]
	quest.1B387FD15E883317.quest_subtitle: "First Tools"
	quest.1B387FD15E883317.title: "Get Some Sort of Tool"
	quest.1B4E42BE6EF7A4F3.quest_desc: [
		"Ore Sorters will take various versions of processed ore and seperate them into valuable materials."
		""
		""
		""
		"Ore Sorting replaces the entire functional ore-processing system of GTCEu:Modern with something closer resembling Angels Ore Processing from Factorio with some liberties taken on design."
		""
		""
		"Ore Chunks (The products of sorting ores at different stages) are your primary sources of materials, and EMI will show you an Ore-Sort diagram any time you click on pure dusts that come from sorting or chunks themselves."
		""
		"I've also removed most of the old raw ores that would have confused you in EMI, so hopefully it's easy to understand and navigate."
		""
		""
		"Ore sorting starts off mildly lossy for T1 and T2 in terms of how many raw ores you put in verses chunks you get out, but as you get higher stages of sorting you also get increased yields. This was notably done because ore fields are massive and offering flat objective multipliers early on and in general caused a lot of resource bloat. (There still is resource bloat regarding how much you get but I'll have to address that over time or just use more materials per craft.)"
	]
	quest.1B4E42BE6EF7A4F3.quest_subtitle: "The heart of ore processing"
	quest.1B801262A2CADD36.quest_desc: ["The steam mixing vessel is a large sized mixer, with the ability to craft up to 4 recipes at a time via parallel. As mentioned with the steam caster, you will need to have the steam to run recipes in tadem."]
	quest.1B801262A2CADD36.quest_subtitle: "Blender go BRRRR"
	quest.1BC8E85866579CF2.quest_desc: ["Next, Take your &eSodium Chromate Solution&r and some &eSulfuric Acid&r and slap that inside a &aChemical Dehydrator&r. You'll end up with &bSodium Dichromate Solution&r and some &6Sodium Sulfate&r as a byproduct."]
	quest.1BC8E85866579CF2.quest_subtitle: "Getting there!"
	quest.1C34FFE7528A8265.quest_desc: [
		"This pickaxe is required to harvest Iesnium trapped in netherrack, if you don't use this pickaxe."
		""
		"&c&lYou will recieve no ores!"
	]
	quest.1C34FFE7528A8265.quest_subtitle: "Mining Iesnium Ore"
	quest.1D9546741C6C9771.quest_desc: [
		"The primitive pump will produce more water based on several factors."
		""
		"The higher general humidity of a biome, the more water it will produce at base."
		""
		"The primitive pump can accept \"Pump Hatches\", ULV Hatches, or LV hatches, each tier of hatch above pump hatch, increases the yield per cycle."
	]
	quest.1D9546741C6C9771.quest_subtitle: "A simple pump"
	quest.1E348A557ECB9BEA.quest_desc: [
		"Will automatically push the contents stored within to your AE2 grid."
		""
		"Basically this removes the step of needing to place an external interface, and avoids the throughput limits of such setups as well."
	]
	quest.1E348A557ECB9BEA.quest_subtitle: "Digital Outputs"
	quest.1FD7F7A22E29CFF5.quest_desc: [
		"Soul Gourd Stems spawn on soul sand or soil in the nether. "
		""
		"This makes Soulsand Valleys a great place to find these!"
		""
		"If you don't have one near your nether access, i'd suggest looking around for soulsand patches near the lava layer"
	]
	quest.1FD7F7A22E29CFF5.quest_subtitle: "Found on soulsand and soil"
	quest.1FECA1C0E8B233D5.quest_desc: ["STORY WORK IS CURRENTLY IN DEV, DEEDS ARE ACTIVE BUT LARGE STORY ENTRIES ARE POSTPONED FOR NOW!"]
	quest.1FECA1C0E8B233D5.quest_subtitle: "{\"translate\":\"deed.cosmiccore.current_flow.subtitle\"}"
	quest.1FECA1C0E8B233D5.title: "{\"translate\":\"deed.cosmiccore.current_flow\"}"
	quest.20110B288860AB9D.quest_subtitle: "Covering and binding."
	quest.203685214E5EDF41.quest_subtitle: "A permanent source of Fluorine"
	quest.20B57C1FF5037C74.quest_desc: [
		"&7This quest desc is a WIP with 90% of them in LV.&r"
		""
		"GregTech Energy (&bEU&r) is split into two features \"&aAmps&r\" and \"&eVolts&r\""
		""
		"&eVoltage&r is the capacity one \"&aAmp&r\" can contain per package of energy."
		""
		"When producing EU, all that matters to you is your EU/t, which is calculated by"
		""
		"(&bEU&r = &eV&r * &aA&r)  "
		"ex, (&b128Eu/t&r = &e32&r * &a4&r) "
		""
		"&l&4NEVER. MIX. VOLTAGES.&r Plugging a higher base voltage into lower-tiered machines will cause an explosion."
		"Example&r : Do not plug a cable carrying &nMV&r &eVoltage&r (&e128 EU per amp&r) into an &nLV&r machine (&e32 EU per amp&r) this will end &cpoorly.&r "
		"Continued on Page 2 : -> (Scroll or Click the Arrow)"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&aAmperage&r (\"&aAmps&r\") is a limit to how much energy a cable can carry."
		"Drawing more than the maximum amps a cable can support will cause it to melt shortly after or start fires. This is &4Also bad&r"
		""
		"If it isn't evident at first, Max &eAmps&r on Wires multiplied by the &avoltage tier&r is the Max &bEU/t&r a cable can support."
	]
	quest.20B57C1FF5037C74.quest_subtitle: "Power Warnings."
	quest.20B57C1FF5037C74.title: "Read this or Explode"
	quest.213495FF52025FAE.quest_desc: ["LV Generator blocks are mostly reserved to outpost establishment, as such they are a bit more costly"]
	quest.213495FF52025FAE.quest_subtitle: "Early Singleblock Generators"
	quest.2167B11F04291D87.quest_desc: [
		"Abyss ores form due to the murkblooms digestive behaviors and extreme pressures of the abyss."
		""
		"Access to &dTitanium&r and &ePlatinum&r have allowed you to produce catalysts that allow your Bloomwyrm algae strand to emulate a similar behavior, crystalizing into metallic formations loosely resembling &aabyssal ores&r."
		""
		"This should allow you to &eautomate them comfortably in your own factory&r, rather than having to continue to &edive for materials&r."
		""
		"While this comes as a relief to you, you suspect you will be back to the abyss in time."
	]
	quest.2167B11F04291D87.quest_subtitle: "Renewability of the Abyss"
	quest.2167B11F04291D87.title: "Industrial Abyss Ores"
	quest.216BBFB436BC4713.quest_desc: [
		"You may use umbral crust alongside some malum spirits to make the same primordial soup, just wastes more hydrofluoric in the process."
		""
		"It's a small sacrifice for the time it spends you hunting the lower Firmament for primordial remnants"
	]
	quest.216BBFB436BC4713.quest_subtitle: "Making the hard part, easier"
	quest.21EC2FF351067FFF.quest_subtitle: "How to get your first (proper) combustion fuels"
	quest.230BE17C3009554C.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you have access to Somarust casings and Stainless steel, it's worth considering upgrading your EBFS to the 2nd tier."
		""
		"Tier 2 EBFS take more space and materials to construct their larger frame, but come with multiple benefits"
		""
		"1. Every recipe that runs will reduce the total duration of the next recipe by 5% up to a max of 50% (half duration)."
		"2. This duration cut also cuts total EU demand in half, saving you 50% of your power, or 2 ingots for the price of one in EU!"
		""
		""
		"The T2 EBF is larger than its sibling T1 EBF, so make sure you got enough space (free in minecraft) "
	]
	quest.230BE17C3009554C.quest_subtitle: "Tier 2"
	quest.230BE17C3009554C.title: "A Better EBF"
	quest.24234FDC4A206DA5.quest_desc: [
		"Computation Arrays allow you to convert &bEU&r (and potentially other resources) into &eComputer Work Units&r. Which we will informally call either &aCWU&r or &aCompute&r."
		""
		""
		"&aCWU&r serves multiple roles, it allows you to connect devices to the network. As well as let those devices run. Passive &aCWU&r demand will always be prioritized before active demand can allocate &aCWU&r"
		""
		""
		"When there is space &aCWU&r and a craft is requested, the craft will attempt to use more than the required &aCWU&r to &bboost production speed&r. This notably means it will attempt to push crafting packages to machines more often. If your machine can keep up, it will keep pushing resources faster and faster."
		""
		""
		"This works great with pattern butters as well(Not actually, it will in the future is the goal, this is mostly to remind myself for that compat later)"
	]
	quest.24234FDC4A206DA5.quest_subtitle: "You need to make one of these."
	quest.24234FDC4A206DA5.title: "Computation for the Network"
	quest.24A51AFDD86B98CA.quest_subtitle: "You know the drill by now."
	quest.24B46F4F68610400.quest_desc: [
		"Will be required to make the first 'Circuit class', Hex Circuits, in HV."
		""
		"For now it's just a faster circuit assembler."
	]
	quest.24B46F4F68610400.quest_subtitle: "Another Circuit Assembler"
	quest.24C8852F25520072.quest_desc: [
		"Future Ore Sorting Tiers will involve fluid logistics, and the recipes are still a wip."
		""
		"For now, they aren't needed, and as such no recipes will be provided for now until i balance their recipes correctly!"
	]
	quest.24C8852F25520072.quest_subtitle: "T4 / 5"
	quest.24C8852F25520072.title: "Coming Soon"
	quest.2631A613ADCD302E.quest_desc: ["Notice, try to avoid putting tools/armor/things with NBT into your stock ticker system, the stock ticker seems to have problems extracting them sometimes."]
	quest.2631A613ADCD302E.quest_subtitle: "A centralized storage"
	quest.2675C878C130E580.quest_subtitle: "Better Netherite"
	quest.2700DA7ED10B4664.quest_desc: [
		"Normally, gregtech spawns veins wildly all over the world at a constant fixed distance in a grid."
		""
		""
		"Frontiers has entirely discared this system for the concept of \"Ore Fields\""
		""
		""
		"Finding a field, you can expect to discover many interconnected veins of the same ore present."
		""
		"Your earliest method of finding fields is the dowsing rod, made from flint, sticks, and string."
		""
		"It will discover the nearest field to you, which you can see on your minimap/world map."
		"To find another, namely different vein, you should walk away from the field you just discovered, as there is a minimum distance between fields"
	]
	quest.2700DA7ED10B4664.quest_subtitle: "How to find resources"
	quest.2700DA7ED10B4664.title: "Ore Fields"
	quest.274F38697C3628FB.quest_desc: ["To move this around safely, you'll want to use either Gold pipes or Drums."]
	quest.274F38697C3628FB.quest_subtitle: "Acid, Careful!"
	quest.27511ADDB495D14D.quest_desc: [
		"This is about the fourth time i've heard someone on discord would eat this, if they could."
		""
		"Please I beg of you, stop eating the metal you need for LV Hulls. Please."
		""
		""
		"Anyway, this insufferable material can only be smelted in your blast furnace and later on, the Electric Blast Furnace. It's slow, so I'd recommend using an IPBF if you aren't."
		""
		""
		"PS. Dwarven Oil helps reduce the crafting time and allows the IPBF to parallel harder, use it."
	]
	quest.27511ADDB495D14D.quest_subtitle: "Stop trying to eat your metals"
	quest.27C5FA2490846E4B.quest_desc: [
		"Take coal and shove it into your pyro ovens. This will produce Coking vapors."
		""
		""
		"Coking Vapors then need to be condensed, their byproducts distilled."
		""
		"Refining coal is generally for Naphthalene which is used later on for various high tier chemistry in EV and IV"
	]
	quest.27C5FA2490846E4B.quest_subtitle: "The root"
	quest.27F49E7BAC5C489F.quest_desc: [
		"Titanium Tetrachloride has a few uses."
		""
		"It can be used for producing Titanium Ingots in an EBF."
		"Or optionally, be used to boost the output of Polymerization processes massively."
		""
		"Some polymers also *require* it in higher tiers (LuV+) so for now you can safely convert it all into titanium without much guilt!"
		""
		""
		"Congratulations for finishing this!"
	]
	quest.27F49E7BAC5C489F.quest_subtitle: "Titanium : Step 5"
	quest.286A2D01AA1775F0.quest_desc: [
		"Electrolyzers allow you to seperate various elements from eachother."
		""
		"Early on, this allows you to get Gallium from your sphalerite, which is vital to progression."
		""
		"Make one."
	]
	quest.286A2D01AA1775F0.quest_subtitle: "Breaking things apart"
	quest.286F950918F4817C.quest_desc: [
		"Vanachrome is located within the 2nd layer of the abyss."
		""
		"Currently you have no reliable way to automatically mine this material as all drills fail in the undergarden due to heavy moisture."
		""
		"For now harvesting ores from the floating stone masses is sufficient, but in the future better sources must be located."
	]
	quest.286F950918F4817C.quest_subtitle: "Raw Chromite Source"
	quest.28CFA2142307F7DC.quest_desc: ["Utherite spawns everywhere in the first abyss layer, harvesting it requires manual mining as"]
	quest.28CFA2142307F7DC.quest_subtitle: "The First Bounty"
	quest.28DD3480F177CBC7.quest_desc: ["Power Relays allow you to insert power into your AE2 grid, as controllers and energy acceptors no longer serve this function."]
	quest.28DD3480F177CBC7.quest_subtitle: "Adding Power to AE"
	quest.2928EF0DCF970AE4.quest_desc: [
		"Fans are extremely powerful in base create."
		""
		"You can wash composite ore with a Create fan to bulk-sift for tiny-dusts from ores if you wish to not manually sift every stack of ore you crush."
		""
		"&cSmelting/Smoking abilities have been disabled&r, as Create fans allow abnormally powerful processing capabilities compared to most if not all GT multis."
		""
		"This was the compromise for letting them be used for literally everything else (including aircraft) instead of gating them to Mid MV like before."
	]
	quest.2928EF0DCF970AE4.quest_subtitle: "A note about Fans."
	quest.2944767D5CF38669.quest_desc: [
		"Most machines are chemically sound in this world, and have no issues surviving."
		"However, most of this land is smeared in a strong arcane interference, most of which will disable machines without proper care taken."
		""
		"This memory fragment seems to respond properly to arcane influx, let's try to use it for machines."
	]
	quest.2944767D5CF38669.quest_subtitle: "Shards of Memory"
	quest.2AA6F78DB2ED60F2.quest_desc: [
		" &7&oYou have dreamed."
		""
		" &7&oA world that was yours, the way you wanted it to be, without flaw, "
		" &7&ogiven your full love"
		""
		" &7&oAlas, this world you made is not for you, it is for the future you have lost.&r"
		""
		" &7&oAwaken."
		""
		""
		" &o&cERROR &7- Inducing Temporal Amnesia has failed.&r"
	]
	quest.2AA6F78DB2ED60F2.quest_subtitle: "We all start somewhere"
	quest.2AA6F78DB2ED60F2.title: "Gather Some Wood"
	quest.2ABEE21EB889B7DD.quest_desc: [
		"Did you know you can throw iron ingots and coal/charcoal dust into lava to batch craft wrought iron?"
		""
		"Give it a try! Wrought Iron is wonderful for early tools!"
	]
	quest.2ABEE21EB889B7DD.quest_subtitle: "Easier Wrought Iron"
	quest.2B4252BD718657DA.quest_desc: [
		"That stuff you use for circuits, in comical amounts."
		""
		""
		"Nice..."
	]
	quest.2B4252BD718657DA.quest_subtitle: "It's Gallium"
	quest.2C681CEA5813573D.quest_subtitle: "Arcane Interference. (Y-400 to Y-600)"
	quest.2C681CEA5813573D.title: "The Hollow Abyss - Layer 3 : Arcantide Sump"
	quest.2CC42A9D4EAB03FF.quest_desc: [
		"Possible in HV with HV Energy Hatches."
		""
		"However, requires a rather well designed petrochemical plant to produce reliably at scale."
		""
		"Gasoline exists, but it's more of a precursor fuel to this or Stardust Infused Gasoline"
	]
	quest.2CC42A9D4EAB03FF.quest_subtitle: "Serious Power Production"
	quest.2DC0CA956B5C4E34.quest_subtitle: "Plastic Trail Mix, the Block"
	quest.2EDDE2D4F167CC02.quest_desc: [
		"You'll need to get some sphalerite first before you can start this step."
		""
		"If you haven't already, look into ore sorting and the tiered progression surrounding it."
		""
		""
		"Also, you can see what ores yield different pure ore chunks in EMI"
		""
		"Yes, this is a mirror of the cobaltite quest description"
		""
		""
		"(Hold a Sphalerite Ore Chunk to Unlock this/Check the Dependencies)"
	]
	quest.2EDDE2D4F167CC02.quest_subtitle: "Have you done ore sorting?"
	quest.2F4C9EE57087AF0E.quest_desc: [
		"You can produce high pressure steam from Large Bronze Boilers."
		""
		"This can be very useful considering how cheap steam power is, it is however not dense enough to use at scale in most cases."
	]
	quest.2F4C9EE57087AF0E.quest_subtitle: "From Large Boilers"
	quest.2F5E6FC176A68A97.quest_desc: [
		"Yes I know there are things like creosote and whatnot or even just the multi-phase oil that can also be burned."
		""
		"Hush, this is the first real deal."
		""
		""
		"Can be useful in Modular Power Substations, as well as it's upgraded Diesel form you may make as soon as you reach an MV mixer."
	]
	quest.2F5E6FC176A68A97.quest_subtitle: "The Earliest Burnable Combustion Fuel"
	quest.2FD2453CE6298D0D.quest_subtitle: "IV Circuit Gate"
	quest.3059236DAE919014.quest_desc: [
		"Wither roses come from a few methods"
		""
		"1. Letting a wither kill you or mobs"
		"2. Some biomes rarely have them, notably the dark forests biomes o plenty has"
	]
	quest.3059236DAE919014.quest_subtitle: "How to get wither roses"
	quest.3099662548BA3F01.quest_subtitle: "Multiblock Deployment"
	quest.309B9C6A20CE437C.quest_desc: [
		"Just as Going down has required some sort of charm to allow passage, throwing myself into the skies most likely carries the same risk."
		""
		"Rather than figuring this out as it happens, I will procure a permit to the skies now rather than later."
	]
	quest.309B9C6A20CE437C.quest_subtitle: "Allowing Passage"
	quest.31B41BDB3296BCF0.quest_desc: ["Allows access to higher tier Neo Vitae recipes and Gregtech recipes, notably, the &6Hemophagic Transfuser"]
	quest.31B41BDB3296BCF0.quest_subtitle: "Tier 3 Blood Orb"
	quest.31B6D09FBE2173EF.quest_desc: [
		"Get down near the bedrock layer and place an ember bore ontop of bedrock, with a mechanical core on the center block, insert coal (or other fuels, haven't tried) into the mechanical core with your logistics of choice (hopper will do). The bore will start to run and produce ember as long as there is ember available for extraction in the chunk"
		""
		""
		"Before you find a place for your bore, you should make an atmospheric gauge, the more the dial increases, the more ember there is"
	]
	quest.31B6D09FBE2173EF.quest_subtitle: "Gathering your First Ember"
	quest.31C9B8A33BD4DB08.quest_desc: [
		"You can extract raw rubber pulp from stick resin, and use some sulfur to create liquid rubber."
		""
		"Infinitely easier to coat cables this way, and it can be fluid solidified into bars/sheets as needed."
	]
	quest.31C9B8A33BD4DB08.quest_subtitle: "Better Rubber Yields"
	quest.31F17F4736AEEAA6.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Hephaestus Cauldron&r is the core of your foundry setup."
		""
		"*slaps roof* this thing produces&b Pyroflux&r, a valuable molten chemical used to refine &eprecious metals into molten alloy mixtures&r."
		""
		"&bAlloy Blast Kilns&r are linked the to cauldron and will consume&b Pyroflux&r steadily while running. "
		""
		""
		"The Cauldron also has several tiers, you can change the preview tier in the structures GUI. "
		"Each tier &eallows more Kilns and other furnances to be linked&r."
		""
		"Tier 1 - &b4 Foundry Devices&r "
		"Tier 2 - &a8 Foundry Devices&r"
		"Tier 3 - &e20 Foundry Devices&r"
		""
		""
		"Each Kiln is as strong as &e4 classic GTCEU Alloy Blast Smelters&r. They are able to parallel, so make sure to &egive them plenty of energy&r!"
		""
		"Heads up, Kilns can also take &afour&r energy hatches! You can feed them a whopping &664A&r of power!"
	]
	quest.31F17F4736AEEAA6.quest_subtitle: "The Foundry of Molten Metals"
	quest.323FAC202CADB824.quest_desc: [
		"Alloys making bronze ingots 4 at a time at the cost of taking steam and time"
		""
		"Same case for Coke Bricks, but also makes them vastly cheaper so it is strongly recommended!"
	]
	quest.323FAC202CADB824.quest_subtitle: "Better Bronze and Coke bricks"
	quest.32A39BA7119B0CB9.quest_desc: [
		"Otherworld Goggles allow you to see the funny invisible ore with your EYES..."
		""
		""
		":)"
	]
	quest.32A39BA7119B0CB9.quest_subtitle: "Useful"
	quest.32CBFA838C794C01.quest_desc: [
		"Allows you to hold all your chalks, and other ritual parts, and allows easy placement of every rune a ritual needs."
		""
		""
		"There is a version of this bag you may create later that will also place the entire ritual at once."
		"This bag can only place individual runes you look at and right click on, when previewing a ritual in world."
	]
	quest.32CBFA838C794C01.quest_subtitle: "Something you might want"
	quest.33A577DB6CA4CEDB.quest_desc: [
		"Malums book is a bit vague at times. the general idea of malum is that you use spirits to make trinkets and rituals that augment the player or world."
		""
		""
		"Firstly your goal is to make some ritual totems, to make the unchained rite to get access to blighted earth."
	]
	quest.33A577DB6CA4CEDB.quest_subtitle: "Crafting Altar of Malum"
	quest.34651919AADD1315.quest_desc: [
		"In short, this page shows"
		""
		"- New Generators above the hull tier they are unlocked at."
		"- Fuel unlocked around a specific energy tier will be listed below their respective hull."
		"- Fuels that are a new tier of the previous will be placed to the right of it's predecessor"
		"- Each fuel has some remark about how it's made, where it sits in progression, and probably some mention on how I neglected it lol. I'll clean this up as I go."
	]
	quest.34651919AADD1315.quest_subtitle: "less confusion, easier understanding!"
	quest.35410493D650E8B5.quest_desc: [
		"The Power Capacitor is a large power buffer that will act as a cushion for many of your hungry production demands."
		""
		"There are times where you simply consume more power than you produce for a breif moment, before you would experience the annoyances of machines shutting off or multiblocks stalling out."
		""
		"A power capacitor fixes this problem by allowing you to push out more amperage than you produce for a limited period of time."
		""
		""
		"Each layer of the power capacitor can house 9 battery blocks that each add individual capacity to the multiblock itself. Eg. 1 LV capacitor will give the multi a capacity of 5 Million EU storage, neat!"
		""
		"You may build up to 5 layers of batteries for a total of 45 battery blocks."
		""
		""
		"In the future, you will have access to a superior version of this multiblock (The Power Substation), but for now this will do."
	]
	quest.35410493D650E8B5.quest_subtitle: "Central Power in earlygame"
	quest.35B7A194BB34BA44.quest_desc: [
		"The \"&6Weirdly Durable Hammer&r\" has infinite durability and can mine obsidian."
		""
		"Like all other tools, it can be buffed massively by enchanting it with efficiency."
		"This is an Optional Quest."
		""
		" &o&#A3A3A3A world stretches before you, wealthy in infinite resources."
		" &o&#A3A3A3Your humble hands struggle to extract enough materials alone."
		" &o&#A3A3A3And thus, whispers remind you of an old lost friend."
		" &o&#A3A3A3And once again, you carve through the world like paper."
	]
	quest.35B7A194BB34BA44.quest_subtitle: "The unsual that is willed to be. "
	quest.35B7A194BB34BA44.title: "An Indestructable Ally"
	quest.35E4FB722A8CA395.quest_desc: [
		"There is currently only one industrial scale power multiblock in Frontiers."
		""
		"The modular power station"
		""
		"Can produce a maximum of 16 Amps, based on the tier of stator contained inside."
		""
		"These will be your bread and butter generators until EV+"
	]
	quest.35E4FB722A8CA395.quest_subtitle: "The Big Power Generator."
	quest.363C62D4C05D712D.quest_desc: [
		"Boilers in Gregtech will require fuel to run, in this case, solid fuel."
		""
		"&cWARNING&r: Do not feed water to a hot dry boiler, it will instantly explode due to flash boiling the water into steam. Fill your boilers with at least some water first before you heat them, to safely avoid this!"
	]
	quest.363C62D4C05D712D.quest_subtitle: "First steam source"
	quest.3640333A3E21701A.title: "Steam and ULV Tier Gear"
	quest.369A6B80AED9D741.quest_subtitle: "The Infinite Sunset"
	quest.369A6B80AED9D741.title: "To HV!"
	quest.369DE54ABB07E98A.quest_desc: [
		"The coke oven allows you to convert logs into charcoal, and coal into coal coke."
		""
		""
		"Worth noting, you will need to make more coke bricks than what you need for assembling a coke oven, as coke bricks are used in a variety of early steam tech."
		""
		"Don't worry, you get better recipes as you go, so the 3x3 shaped craft is only for starting out."
	]
	quest.369DE54ABB07E98A.quest_subtitle: "Coking coals"
	quest.369DE54ABB07E98A.title: "Coke Oven and Coke Bricks"
	quest.369F4EE8B47CD89F.quest_desc: [
		"stick an ember receptor on one of the bottom faces of the melter, and link it to an injector on your ember source."
		""
		"next, put your item in the top, and watch it melt down into a fluid!"
		"You can pipe this out in any way you wish, be it embers pipes or gt pipes."
	]
	quest.369F4EE8B47CD89F.quest_subtitle: "Using that ember"
	quest.3733906CF47B1C06.quest_subtitle: "Multipurpose and cheap"
	quest.373DE13547832AB8.quest_desc: [
		"One of your goals this chapter is reaching MV circuits. This will require some extensive work to get to."
		""
		""
		"1. &bEBF&r : You will need for creating Dark Steel and Soul Stained Steel needed for LV Field Gens."
		"2. &bAra Vitae&r : Required to make some of the chalks needed for Runed Steel."
		"3. &bOre Sorting&r : While not strictly required to get gallium, it is strictly required for arsenic for diodes."
		""
		""
		""
		"Once you have made your first &aMV circuits&r, it is strongly recommended to invest them into the &eCircuit Assembler&r, which is the most expensive singleblock of any tier, usually granting higher tier circuit crafts or shortcuts for current circuit recipes."
	]
	quest.373DE13547832AB8.quest_subtitle: "Getting your first MV Circuit!"
	quest.3783BCAAC66A76E1.quest_desc: [
		"The Bronze Steam turbine allows you to insert a turbine rotor alongside your steam to produce >4A of LV power per multiblock."
		""
		"Turbine Rotors are now indestructible, and do not take damage."
		"Steel Turbine Rotors are a good starting point."
		""
		""
		"You will need to produce higher energy dynamos than you can propable produce presently. "
		"Bronze Turbines can accept up to 16A LV dynamos"
	]
	quest.3783BCAAC66A76E1.quest_subtitle: "Your First Power Source"
	quest.37C177A6C62CEDE0.quest_desc: [
		"Neutralize your Red Mud from a basic solution using some Hydrochloric Acid."
		""
		"Neutralized Red Mud is able to then be centrifuged further into Red Mud Slurry."
		""
		"You're almost done!"
	]
	quest.37C177A6C62CEDE0.quest_subtitle: "Titanium : Step 3"
	quest.37C1E726B179C65E.quest_desc: ["Steel Rotors mean each Turbine costs more steel upfront, but each turbine will also produce more power!"]
	quest.37C1E726B179C65E.quest_subtitle: "A Recommendation"
	quest.38473AAE9EFA91C7.quest_desc: [
		"Ember is easy to move!"
		""
		"Just place an Ember Emitter onto your source of embers, and connected it to an ember receptor with a tinker hammer."
	]
	quest.38473AAE9EFA91C7.quest_subtitle: "Moving Ember"
	quest.391A834FBA98B236.quest_subtitle: "Moving Rotation"
	quest.3986D39DC5DCFEE1.quest_desc: [
		"Frontiers foregos the standard GTModern Worldgen for something closer to massive ore fields roughly inspired by Factorio."
		""
		"Fields are &6marked on the map&r when prospected, and can be toggled for depletion."
		"Fields are &eautomatically shared between team members&r."
		"Fields generally try to spawn in a way that &6eliminates pure RNG&r "
		""
		"Details regarding how to locate veins inside of fields, as well as information on the RNG behavior can be found on the "
		"&cNEXT PAGE &c[CLICK THE ARROW, BOTTOM RIGHT] &r"
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"&e&lRNG&r"
		""
		"RNG usesthe concept of a shuffle bag (Inspired off Tetris) to keep roughly all the ores spawning within a specific region."
		"You can make a &bDowsing Rod&r the moment you find some string! Use it as it is very helpful early on!"
		""
		"&l&eLocating the Ore, a quick crashcourse&r:"
		""
		"Generally, the logical '&bcenter&r' of an ore blob has an extremely high chance to intersect with the ore field in some way."
		""
		"Personally I &alocate the center then dig down directly&r, but you can also dig tunnels down to the center. "
		"You can check &eEMI&r to see a rough area where yeah field will spawn. Once you've found some of the field you most likely will never need to hunt for any other piece of it as fields are HUGE."
	]
	quest.3986D39DC5DCFEE1.quest_subtitle: "Ore Fields and You"
	quest.3986D39DC5DCFEE1.title: "Reworked Ore Generation"
	quest.3A755F7B8012AB1A.quest_subtitle: "Create Oxygen Tank"
	quest.3B848C1CC6779862.quest_desc: [
		"This for the time being is a byproduct until you are more situated into EV."
		""
		""
		"This is where you start getting materials like Iridium, Osmium, Ruthenium, and Rhodium."
	]
	quest.3B848C1CC6779862.quest_subtitle: "IMPORTANT, SAVE IT! ! !"
	quest.3BB0BE543EA4AAD4.quest_desc: [
		"Bauxite produces a massive amount of Aluminium, Gallium, Rutile, and various trace materials."
		""
		""
		"The following quests ahead show each step you should focus on as you assemble this chain."
		""
		"Descriptions will be kept mostly short as by now you should be familiar enough with EMI to navigate this. Each product ahead follows the primary step throughout the chain."
		""
		"Goodluck!"
	]
	quest.3BB0BE543EA4AAD4.quest_subtitle: "Your First Titanium Source"
	quest.3CE82619B0AEEC42.quest_desc: [
		"Horray! Rutile! This is Titanium Oxide, a precursor to your actual Titanium Metal."
		""
		"You will need to process it with a bit of Chlorine and Carbon to get Titanium Tetrachloride"
		"&l"
	]
	quest.3CE82619B0AEEC42.quest_subtitle: "Titanium : Step 4"
	quest.3D236794B8757616.quest_desc: [
		"The &aLeyline Orrery&r is the companion tool of the &eLeyline Compressor&r, allowing you to access and easily deploy any leyline patterns within your AE2 system."
		""
		"Shift+R-Click your Orrery to open the UI. "
		""
		"This Interface may feel confusing at first, but it's rather easy once you've gotten used to it."
		""
		"At the top, you have &b8 input slots&r, you may set &aany encoded structure pattern&r to these slots."
		"Holding the radial key [Default:R] will allow you to quickly access anything defined to those slots."
		""
		"If you have the appropriate leyline package in your AE2 system, you may &bsummon that multiblock in world with&r your Orrery."
		""
		"The Orrery also has &a4 total config sets&r, each config set can hold &b8 multi imprints&r, for a total of &e32 quick binds&r for an Orrery."
		""
		"Orrerys are directly linked in &eAE2 wireless access points&r, and also have the option to &drequest crafting&r of leyline packages if you happen to run out."
		""
		""
		"&7This tool is currently under heavy development, the basics work, but things like deconstruction, rotation for placement, and wallsharing/clipping into similar blocks are WIP. It is still massively useful for slamming down entire large mutliblock setups into the world at once.&r"
	]
	quest.3D236794B8757616.quest_subtitle: "Bind to the will of Magic"
	quest.3D90267D6A7C7CF8.quest_desc: [
		"Weak blood shards imbue the nature of Anima and Gravglass, however they can also be procured from slain mobs if desperate."
		""
		"Either go raid the firmament for Gravitic Faultstone or stab mobs with a sentient blade"
	]
	quest.3D90267D6A7C7CF8.quest_subtitle: "A shard of something larger"
	quest.3DB50B6AD89CBB9D.quest_desc: [
		"Allows you to craft blocks of metal, as well as compress nuggets into ingots."
		""
		"Not as important as other machines, but still finds its uses, you'll still need one..."
	]
	quest.3DB50B6AD89CBB9D.quest_subtitle: "Squishing things"
	quest.3DF01B41E0E692A6.quest_desc: [
		"Combine Sodium Hydroxide Solution, Silicon Dioxide, and Bauxite in a mixer."
		""
		"This will make your bauxite solution"
	]
	quest.3DF01B41E0E692A6.quest_subtitle: "Titanium : Step 1"
	quest.3E03C13CAE570D80.quest_desc: ["You can also get quartz blocks from stone masons, which allows you to make this pre-nether!"]
	quest.3E03C13CAE570D80.quest_subtitle: "Stone Mason Source"
	quest.3E42DDEBA9DBB13C.quest_desc: [
		"The second layer of the abyss seems to be populated more densely with biomass than the first layer."
		""
		"This indicates the first layer is notably some kind of &nfeeding ground&r for a large organism or many smaller organisms."
		""
		"I would assume the Murkbloom consumes biomass at the surface and then sinks back down to deeper layers and &9provides nutrients to the rockbed&r."
		""
		"I should be careful, my passive sonars are detecting &6unusual spikes of activity in the water&r. It's safe to assume the density of Murkbloom here is higher, and more agressive to the sounds I make."
		""
		"I should consider researching the plantlife within the first layer of the Hollowed Abyss, they may allow me to mimic their sound supressing biology."
	]
	quest.3E42DDEBA9DBB13C.quest_subtitle: "Biodiversity in the fog. (Y-200 to Y-400)"
	quest.3E42DDEBA9DBB13C.title: "The Hollow Abyss - Layer 2 : Muted Shelves"
	quest.3E814BEF0F9709DF.quest_desc: [
		"The integral frameworks are used to create a stable frame for your machine casings."
		""
		"houses all the other electrical and aracane attuned junk a machine hull needs to not violently explode."
	]
	quest.3E814BEF0F9709DF.quest_subtitle: "The frames the core"
	quest.3FB852AA4A2FBB8B.quest_desc: [
		"Primitive Pumps allow passive collection of water."
		""
		""
		"If you haven't i'd recommend making one to automatically fill your boilers before you start!"
	]
	quest.3FB852AA4A2FBB8B.quest_subtitle: "Did you make a pump?"
	quest.400AE9FA07D9F107.quest_subtitle: "Optionally, Denser Storage"
	quest.40646DECFE17F19E.quest_desc: [
		"You can create pure gemstones by using a pile of explosives inside of an implosion compressor."
		""
		"You can automate tnt early on with powdercane before you have access to toluene"
	]
	quest.40646DECFE17F19E.quest_subtitle: "Where's all the gems?"
	quest.40E9979B215578FF.quest_desc: [
		"There's a few ways to get chlorine, but one of your earliest options is electrolyzing salt from earthen salt veins."
		""
		"By now you most likely have a variety of salt types from ore sorting, any one that contains Chlorine will do fine. Otherwise you may smelt earthen salts directly into rock salt and use that in dust form."
	]
	quest.40E9979B215578FF.quest_subtitle: "How do I get this stuff?"
	quest.426AD0428F04EB96.quest_desc: [
		"Cetane Boosted Diesel takes your diesel even farther by nearly doubling the power density."
		""
		"I'd recommend making this before starting proper oil refinement, or look into Pure Cinder Gas (once i give it a recipe)."
	]
	quest.426AD0428F04EB96.quest_subtitle: "Oh thats... Quite powerful."
	quest.4290CE767687C140.title: "Oils, So many, Oils!?!?!"
	quest.435306F53E3CCA44.quest_subtitle: "The Gamechanger"
	quest.43C63859BA47960F.quest_desc: ["Worth noting, you'll be able to make this renewably late HV, so keep that in mind!"]
	quest.4425184AA625FA4E.quest_desc: [
		"Looks like it'd taste like extremely tart blue raspberry"
		""
		""
		"I would strongly recommend mining enough of this to make an Iesnium Pickaxe and a Dimensional Mineshaft."
		""
		"These two combined will allow passive production of Iesnium that doesn't need annoying mining methods to locate."
		""
		""
		"In HV, you will also gain a mechanical version of the dimensional mineshaft that can produce otherworld materials at an industrial scale, Nice!"
	]
	quest.4425184AA625FA4E.quest_subtitle: "This looks edible"
	quest.448F8668DD3AEB72.quest_desc: [
		"As you've been playing, you most likely noticed many foods have a stat on them that says something like..."
		""
		"&e\"Main Course\""
		"&e\"Side\""
		"&e\"Drink\""
		""
		""
		"These are the 3 Food Classifications that exist for &ocreating meals&r, and all meals start with a &emain course&r."
		""
		"Right click your main course of choice onto the hearth plate, and optionally add a side and drink."
		"When you are ready. Eat your food by &nright clicking&r. Your meal will become a great memory!"
		""
		"You may have 1 memorized meal active at a time, and it will last until you die or eat another meal. You will get the combined stats of the entire meal as a permanent buff until then. (A way to see the combined buff will be in a future UI addition, most likely hovering over the icon itself)"
		""
		""
		"Eating a variety of meals increases your taste profile, the more unique meals you've consumed oveer time, the stronger the impact of meals becomes. New meals only get added to your taste profile once per minecraft day, so you can only improve this by trying meals often."
		""
		"Eating the same meal over and over will eventually make it a \"Signature Meal\", which will prompt the player to shift-right-click their empty plate after a qualifiying meal, Signature meals are permanent and will grant you a portion of their stats forever, even after dying."
		""
		"&6"
		"UIs for tracking your pallete/taste profile and Signature meals will come in a future update along with another system which can house their GUI elements.&r"
	]
	quest.448F8668DD3AEB72.quest_subtitle: "A meal to remember"
	quest.44E9E456C064F01F.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you have access to Somarust casings and Stainless steel, it's worth considering upgrading your EBFS to the 2nd tier."
		""
		"Tier 2 EBFS take more space and materials to construct their larger frame, but come with multiple benefits"
		""
		"1. Every recipe that runs will reduce the total duration of the next recipe by 5% up to a max of 50% (half duration)."
		"2. This duration cut also cuts total EU demand in half, saving you 50% of your power, or 2 ingots for the price of one in EU!"
		"3. Upon Reaching Max Discount, it will also grant 1 free parallel, useful when you're smelting on-tier voltage ingots that you can do 2 at a time with a standard energy hatch."
		""
		"The T2 EBF is larger than its sibling T1 EBF, so make sure you got enough space (free in minecraft) "
	]
	quest.44E9E456C064F01F.quest_subtitle: "A Better EBF"
	quest.44E9E456C064F01F.title: "Tier 2 EBF"
	quest.44F40A00C61EFE54.quest_desc: [
		"Silicon Ingots Require Kanthal Coils as well as a way to cool the hot ingots down."
		""
		"If you haven't already, this would be the time to make an MV Chemical Bath."
	]
	quest.44F40A00C61EFE54.quest_subtitle: "Requires Kanthal Coils"
	quest.46025BCA76960F68.quest_desc: [
		"You'll need to get some cobaltite first before you can start this step."
		""
		"If you haven't already, look into ore sorting and the tiered progression surrounding it."
		""
		""
		"Also, you can see what ores yield different pure ore chunks in EMI"
		""
		"Yes this is a mirror of the sphalerite quest description."
		""
		"(Hold a Cobaltite Ore Chunk to Unlock this/Check the Dependencies)"
	]
	quest.46025BCA76960F68.quest_subtitle: "Have you done ore sorting?"
	quest.4640766C36B5DCE4.quest_desc: [
		"Hi, if you managed to reach this quest, congrats you beat the- wait no."
		""
		""
		"You've completed the pack to the current development tier associated with the release 0.8.0."
		""
		"From this point forward, anything past here is considered extremely in dev or alpha content that may"
		""
		"- Break"
		"- Vanish without warning"
		"- Be changed without warning"
		"- Any combination of the above, and thensome."
		""
		"Note: If you would like to follow along with the live in-dev version of the pack, head over to the discord (or github) and pick up an 0.9.0-Nightly-### release to try out content and updates beyond this point. Otherwise you will have to wait for 8.X for patches/updates/etc, which will come out as deemed relevant"
	]
	quest.4640766C36B5DCE4.quest_subtitle: "0.9.0 Content"
	quest.4650821FD91027D7.quest_desc: [
		"You notice a crushing feeling effect you as you swim closer to Y:-200."
		""
		"You suspect you will need some stronger armor with pressure resistance as you decend."
		""
		"Hydraulic Armor is the first tier of modular armor you have access to and is capable of holding"
		"a &6Pressure Module I&r, this will allow you to survive up to -400m in the Hollowed Abyss"
	]
	quest.4650821FD91027D7.quest_subtitle: "Your ticket to Layer 2"
	quest.4650821FD91027D7.title: "Hydraulic Armor"
	quest.469D5D2740B79048.quest_desc: [
		"The powderizer will convert purified ores into a finely ground dust for chemical sepperation."
		""
		"Sorting the ground dust will give you the same outputs as regular purified ore sorting does."
		""
		"At this point most of the mechanical seperation steps you can take have been done. The next step requires chemical treatments. I would recommend you get a reliable source of Polyethylene before upgrading further"
	]
	quest.469D5D2740B79048.quest_subtitle: "Finely Ground (Tier 2 Ore Processing)"
	quest.46A8D660ABEB83FA.quest_desc: [
		"&eBronze&r is useful for crafting rudimentary frames and parts for machines."
		""
		""
		"The earliest method you have is using a &6mortar&r to shred your copper ingots and tin nuggets into dust, and then crafting those into bronze."
		""
		"Once you have access to a &6compressor&r and &6alloy smelter&r, you can make bronze much more efficiently."
		""
		""
		""
		""
		"You will need a LOT of bronze, gather as much copper as you can."
		"I'd recommend finding a trial chamber and scrapping the copper from it. "
		"...or an Cuprosiva Ore Field."
	]
	quest.46A8D660ABEB83FA.quest_subtitle: "The First Alloy"
	quest.47BD8BE2ED778B42.quest_subtitle: "Option One: Neo Vitae"
	quest.48EB53B52F2FC7D5.quest_desc: [
		"Indium is usually very difficult to source, a bonus yield of indium from Sphalarite extraction should help you stockpile enough before it is needed in IV+"
		""
		"The Cadmium and Gallium are also nice bonuses"
	]
	quest.48EB53B52F2FC7D5.quest_subtitle: "Oh nice!"
	quest.48EB53B52F2FC7D5.title: "Extra Goodies!"
	quest.491CDA85270DF154.quest_desc: [
		"While not strictly required, this helps you recover various inputs you just spent producing red mud."
		""
		"When I mean it's not strictly required, there is a good chance both Silicon Dixoide and Sodium Hydroxide you can fully passive at fast enough speeds for the waste of it to not matter."
		""
		""
		"It is up to you if you wish to extra the extra aluminium or gallium this yields."
	]
	quest.491CDA85270DF154.quest_subtitle: "Recycling options"
	quest.4978BF804A8975F5.quest_desc: [
		"SU is still produced normally as it would be in standard create."
		""
		"Waterwheels, Wind Mills, and Steam Engines."
		""
		""
		"Hold W to ponder most anything from create for more detailed info on the block itself."
	]
	quest.4978BF804A8975F5.quest_subtitle: "Base Create Behavior"
	quest.4978BF804A8975F5.title: "Generating SU"
	quest.49A607F0508C8F58.quest_subtitle: "TODO: WIP CONTENT"
	quest.49FC9BA649059B12.quest_desc: [
		"That wasn't so hard, was it?"
		""
		"PTFE brings you closer to one of the best machines in the game"
		""
		"The \"&6Large Chemical Reactor&r\""
		""
		"Let's work on making one now"
	]
	quest.49FC9BA649059B12.quest_subtitle: "PTFE"
	quest.4A608CA30FD3D86D.quest_desc: [
		"Silver can be hand sorted from Crushed Galenite ore by hand or washed with a create fan."
		""
		""
		"It is, however, strongly recommended to set up ore sorting. As ore sorting, even just the first few tiers, vastly increases acquisition sources on many materials you will need from this point on."
	]
	quest.4A608CA30FD3D86D.quest_subtitle: "Sources of Silver"
	quest.4A90C6B25FC79EAC.quest_desc: [
		"Stick this down, hopper ember shards/crystals in, watch it turn into ember"
		""
		"use the tinkers hammer on ember emitters/receptors to link them together."
	]
	quest.4A90C6B25FC79EAC.quest_subtitle: "Activating Ember"
	quest.4AA12DEF3B9ED6D2.quest_desc: [
		"Sit's on par with Cetane Boosted Diesel, if only falling behind a little short at 1760 EU/mb verses Cetanes 2160."
		""
		""
		"Both are renewable, just one is much easier to scale, and it's most likely TBSD.(Thunder Boosted Source Diesel) compared to cetane"
	]
	quest.4AA12DEF3B9ED6D2.quest_subtitle: "Oh."
	quest.4B6C5108309A0926.quest_subtitle: "NYI"
	quest.4B8BB9D41D0D0652.quest_desc: [
		"AE2 devices, when attached to a AE2 network, consume 'channels'. "
		""
		"Channels are a &6soft-limiter&r to how many devices can be on a cable at once."
		""
		"For smart cables this is &a16&r, and dense cables this is &a64&r. You may connect as many devices to a cable as you wish, the only cost is extra CWU demand."
		""
		""
		"Going over the soft cap will incur a &ncompounding CWU cost&r for every new component."
		"As a result, it's recommended you &npractice good cable managment&r to keep your channels split and capacity under overload thresholds."
		""
		"Granted, this is a suggestion if you are willing to scale CWU hard enough... (Like, really hard)"
		""
		""
		"&7Due to the nature and complexity of the entire CWU system being a cornerstone mechanic of the pack, you can no longer control/disable the size/state of channels.&r"
	]
	quest.4B8BB9D41D0D0652.quest_subtitle: "Importance of channels"
	quest.4B8BB9D41D0D0652.title: "New Channel System: Cable Overloads"
	quest.4BA1283454E50D62.quest_desc: [
		"ME Drives are used to house all your ME Drives, the things that hold your items and fluids digitally."
		""
		""
		"You will notice they have a few numbers, a 'byte' value and a 'type value"
		""
		"types - each unique item in a drive consumes 1 type count, unstackables consume 1 type per."
		""
		"bytes - the total storage of the drive, more bytes means more items can be held."
		""
		""
		"One thing to note: Drives store items more efficiently if there are less types in the drive. Each unique item in a drive reserves a portion of the drive for that type and lowers the max total stacks a drive can store. This matters if you want to store large volumes of singular items/fluids in drives."
	]
	quest.4BA1283454E50D62.quest_subtitle: "Digital Storage Storage"
	quest.4C8AB307C45DBC3C.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.4C8AB307C45DBC3C.quest_subtitle: "Into the Undergarden"
	quest.4C8AB307C45DBC3C.title: "Below Hell, The Undergarden"
	quest.4CBACE925D480CAA.quest_desc: [
		"When entering the deepslate level of the world, the air will become too thin to breathe normally."
		""
		"To aide in this, you can craft several items that counter air loss"
		""
		"Rebreather : Will double your air-capacity in thin-air environments"
		""
		"Reinforced Rebreather : Will halt oxygen loss in thin air and no air environments as long as you have a valid Oxygen Supply Tank (Bronze or Steel) "
		""
		"Create Backtank : Also compatible with the Reinforced Rebreather for pre-oxygen usage."
		""
		""
		""
		"For environments inside of water, you will have to use a Diving Helmet + Tanks of your choice."
		"This might not work/apply in all cases, please let me know if you find strange places you can/can't breathe when you should/shouldn't be able to!"
	]
	quest.4CBACE925D480CAA.quest_subtitle: "Breathing in places you can't"
	quest.4D779318D62835EC.quest_desc: ["TODO: WIP CONTENT"]
