	quest.4D779318D62835EC.title: "To Beyond the Clouds"
	quest.4E3A7CB013A59A37.quest_desc: ["You can now use concrete to produce coke bricks more efficiently!"]
	quest.4E3A7CB013A59A37.quest_subtitle: "Better Coke Brick Recipe"
	quest.4EAF13E3E6637002.quest_desc: [
		"Wrapping the pearls alongside the memory fragments in tempered iesnium creates a small clockwork core capable of reliably syncing machines to the worlds arcane waves."
		""
		""
		"This behavior seems similar to some kind of wave cancelation."
	]
	quest.4EAF13E3E6637002.quest_subtitle: "Memorized Arcane Rhythm"
	quest.4EC14E444BA1DE40.quest_subtitle: "The first source"
	quest.50930E8761259EFD.quest_desc: [
		"It says parallel, but it's more like 'batch processing'"
		""
		""
		"the more dense and faster the recipe, the better return per ingot of steel is"
		""
		""
		"Best combo (Wrought Iron Block + Coke Block) will result in about a 50% duration cut per steel ingot!"
	]
	quest.50930E8761259EFD.quest_subtitle: "The tooltip lies"
	quest.50A60E8F488274DF.quest_subtitle: "Flocculation Solution"
	quest.50E6647866944CB9.quest_desc: [
		"Gold runes written from yellow chalk."
		""
		"You'll need this to draw the rituals needed to produce the next tier of chalk, &aLime"
	]
	quest.50E6647866944CB9.quest_subtitle: "Another Color"
	quest.51300168EE4A12AB.quest_subtitle: "Optionally, another source"
	quest.5156A433A39D8C82.quest_desc: ["Can be distilled from biomass at a distillery. There are multiple methods to produce biomass, I will leave it up to you to figure out what works for you the best."]
	quest.5156A433A39D8C82.quest_subtitle: "The other orange fluid, besides Sulfuric Acid"
	quest.529FD249F9581506.quest_desc: [
		"Treated planks are needed to craft the primitive pump."
		""
		"They also are a great way to burn through creosote if you have too much, granted that might be better for boilers..."
	]
	quest.529FD249F9581506.quest_subtitle: "It's in the name."
	quest.5345A254BA73F18E.quest_desc: [
		"After learning you can spatially compress materials into denser forms, you imagined the same for &6Multiblocks&r."
		""
		"Leyline packages (name pending) allow you to store entire pre-built multiblocks ready for rapid deployment and keeping inventory clutter free."
		""
		"You can access this feature in HV, with Autocrafting, it is currently here to serve as a reminder for when i build HV LOL"
	]
	quest.5345A254BA73F18E.quest_subtitle: "The Ultimate Deployment Tool"
	quest.5345A254BA73F18E.title: "Leyline Packages"
	quest.53497D07DA7DC94B.quest_desc: ["Loaded Metal Medium is not too difficult, bar the consumption of nyctophyte..."]
	quest.53497D07DA7DC94B.quest_subtitle: "Heavy Metals"
	quest.534DBCED4E339D89.quest_desc: [
		"Stick an Ember receptor on it, and an ember emitter on your ember source."
		""
		"Use the Tinkering Hammer to connect them."
		""
		""
		"This is a pretty temporary recipe until i can be asked to make Steam Ember Hatches."
	]
	quest.534DBCED4E339D89.quest_subtitle: "Getting Embers into a Gregtech Machine"
	quest.53930C8D5E0254CF.quest_desc: [
		"You will need, a LOT of this stuff."
		""
		"Like, a few hours worth of smelting a lot of this stuff."
		""
		"It may be within your best interests to make a 2nd or 3rd EBF if you haven't."
	]
	quest.53930C8D5E0254CF.quest_subtitle: "Oh boy"
	quest.5409781BE86F8DA3.quest_desc: [
		"You already spent the energy making ethylene in LV or at least sometime in MV."
		""
		"You'll need PVC to make the cladding used for HV Casings."
		""
		""
		"So what are you waiting for, go make some! It's also useful for some cable recipes too!"
	]
	quest.5409781BE86F8DA3.quest_subtitle: "You should be able to make this"
	quest.5461D8E87350BBA2.quest_desc: [
		"The Steam Caster is a large multiblock solidifier, it can do up to 4 recipes at a time via parallel, granted you provide it enough steam."
		""
		""
		"You'll need to use this multiblock to produce Firebricks, your next goal. They are required for high pressure boilers/steam machines as well as making steel in the Primitive Blast Furnace."
	]
	quest.5461D8E87350BBA2.quest_subtitle: "Solidifying products"
	quest.54B49FEDB84237C0.quest_desc: ["You will need massive amounts of clay for Andesite Alloy and Fireclay, gather at least 4 stacks."]
	quest.54B49FEDB84237C0.quest_subtitle: "Get a bunch of this"
	quest.5505401B1E8344EB.quest_subtitle: "The Key to Steel"
	quest.55175CA92EB687C4.quest_desc: [
		"Welcom to the first &6Campus Multiblock&r!"
		""
		"*checks notes*"
		"Uh"
		""
		"To keep it simple, the following machines are apart of the \"Murkbloom Heart\" Network"
		""
		"- Sculk Biochamber"
		"- Abyssal Culture Vat"
		"- the 3 others i need to write here but forgot."
		""
		""
		"link them together using datasticks, right click your bloomwyrm heart and then right click the related controller."
		""
		""
		""
		"The Heart provides power, biopower, and bloomwyrm charge to relevant machines, nifty right?"
	]
	quest.55175CA92EB687C4.quest_subtitle: "The core of Biological Processing"
	quest.569024DB10BE8F59.quest_desc: ["If you are unaware of what fuels exist, go check out the fuel tab in the general advice tab at the bottom of the questbook!"]
	quest.569024DB10BE8F59.quest_subtitle: "Fuel choices"
	quest.57BB16A689D2F0B2.quest_desc: [
		"You will need at least HV Energy hatches to work with this material."
		""
		"It also is much more looped and produces many byproducts you have already encountered."
		""
		"I will save you the trouble of making you handle more quests with it."
	]
	quest.57BB16A689D2F0B2.quest_subtitle: "EV power required!"
	quest.57E59B0060EAB2C7.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to Cosmic Frontiers, we're glad to have you here."
		""
		"This quest is to get some housekeeping and information out of the way that's important to remember while playing Frontiers."
		""
		"1. &6We heavily modify the content of many mods, to the point that bug reports should not be submitted to mod devs. Please report &lALL&r &6issues to the modpack Github Firstly.&r"
		"Reporting issues/crashes from this pack to mod devs may waste their time on mechanics that are pack exclusive and aren't relevant anywhere else."
		""
		"&bModpack Github&r : https://github.com/Frontiers-PackForge/CosmicFrontiers/issues"
		"&bModpack Discord&r : https://discord.com/invite/fkxPAq9VQp"
		""
		"2. &eThis modpack has a built in narrative and story, quest chapters automatically appear when you reach major goals in the previous chapter.&r"
		"&4&lBE WARNED: Enabling Edit Mode in the questbook may spoil the suprise."
		""
		"3. When you are ready to begin, head over to the Steam Age Chapter"
		""
		"Dev Note :"
		"&aThe pack is currently in active development, and has recently migrated to 1.21."
		"&aQuestbook will be improved as development goes along!&r"
		"&aCore Mechanics and descriptions of them will be added here in time."
		"&aCheck back on this page as I will add guides here over time!"
	]
	quest.57E59B0060EAB2C7.quest_subtitle: "Welcome to Frontiers"
	quest.57E59B0060EAB2C7.title: "Welcome to Cosmic Frontiers"
	quest.581145B56BCEB344.quest_desc: [
		"Make some circuits, you'll need a pile of these before reaching LV."
		""
		""
		"Make 64 of them, feel free to snack on some as well, you'll have to make more, though."
	]
	quest.581145B56BCEB344.quest_subtitle: "Mmmm, Crunchy..."
	quest.581145B56BCEB344.title: "Circuits Galore"
	quest.5932B46BC3A3AF35.quest_subtitle: "Algae, we love Algae"
	quest.5973534E85F5D126.quest_subtitle: "Better Iesnium"
	quest.599DB6B01E4EA14D.quest_desc: [
		"You quite literally just put a chili pepper in hydrochloric and mixed it into your fuel."
		""
		"What? Sure whatever, it makes more EU per milibucket."
	]
	quest.599DB6B01E4EA14D.quest_subtitle: "Making it Spicy"
	quest.59AE67A4364865C2.quest_desc: [
		"Diesel can be made with Middle Fraction Distillates and Gas Oils, both of which can come from the simple desalter. "
		""
		""
		"Just until now you lacked the braincells and machine tier to mix them together."
		"Do that now, go make some gas oils and blend it into Diesel, it'll make your fuel last MUCH longer."
	]
	quest.59AE67A4364865C2.quest_subtitle: "MV Mixer Gated"
	quest.5B91A99F1F8B588D.quest_desc: [
		"You now have access to a source of sphalerite (zinc) in the nether, and can create brass."
		""
		"This is notably useful for Create machines as well as the few GT machines that require it."
		""
		"To get it, hand sort &ecrushed pyrolitic ore&r"
	]
	quest.5B91A99F1F8B588D.quest_subtitle: "Oh hey, brass!"
	quest.5C931C1E3917BC14.quest_desc: [
		"For the Cost of 28mb/t of steam, you can shred down 8 items at a time with a Steam Grinder."
		"A single steam ginder allows you to effectively double your resource yield, given you have the steam to power it! Useful for stretching your resources farther :)"
		""
		"This is a Multiblock, Check EMI for building instructions on what hatches you need, or shift-right-click the controller in world to see a ghost preview and a layer by layer guide (duration may be controlled in GT's Config settings)"
		""
		""
		"For the Steam Grinder you will need"
		"- A &aSteam Input Hatch&r (Not a &cFluid Input Hatch (Steam)&r)"
		"- A &aSteam Input Bus&r"
		"- A &aSteam Output Bus&r"
		"- The Actual &aSteam Grinder Controller&r"
		"- 22 &aSteam Machine Casings&r (&eNot including casings used in crafts!&r)"
		""
		"&bNOTE&r: &eJust like all &r<&6HV&r &eMacerators, it does not yield byproducts &r(&bSlots 2-4 in EMI&r)"
	]
	quest.5C931C1E3917BC14.quest_subtitle: "A Bigger Macerator"
	quest.5CAF8B02C3FE99ED.quest_desc: ["After that get your &eSodium Dichromate Solution&r, and add some &eCarbon&r with it inside a &achemical dehydrator&r again. This should yield you some &bChromium (III) Oxide&r as well as byproducts of &6Soda Ash&r and &6Carbon Monoxide&r"]
	quest.5CAF8B02C3FE99ED.quest_subtitle: "Almost..."
	quest.5E1DF9CD2C9197EB.quest_desc: [
		"First up we need to make the chromite a solution."
		"Take &eChromite&r, &eOxygen&r, and &eSodium Cabonate Solution&r and react them in a &achemical reactor&r."
		""
		"This will give you &bSodium Chromate Solution&r, as well as &6Magnetite&r and &6CO2&r as Byproducts."
	]
	quest.5E1DF9CD2C9197EB.quest_subtitle: "Needs some more work."
	quest.5E23F46CA23B9EF0.quest_desc: [
		"if you haven't already, you might be sitting on a huge backlog of dwarven oils."
		""
		"You can optionally turn it into inert cinder gas, which is the precursor to this, Cindergas."
	]
	quest.5E23F46CA23B9EF0.quest_subtitle: "Using all that Dwarven Oil"
	quest.5E380EE48FCB8769.quest_desc: [
		"The Ara Vitae is the parallel to BloodMagic's Blood Altar."
		""
		"It can be filled by shift+clicking on it with an orb"
		""
		"It will damage the player for 1 Heart and fill the altar with Essentia Vitae."
		""
		"Be careful! This can &ckill you&r! I'd strongly recommend loading up on the &ahighest quality foods&r you can make (For more HP/Faster Regen when it triggers) as well as investing into some form of &dhealing/regen&r that isn't strictly your passive recovery."
		""
		"This is the difference between this being &ctedious as hell&r and &emildly managable&r until you an automate Essentia Vitae."
	]
	quest.5E380EE48FCB8769.quest_subtitle: "The Altar of Life"
	quest.5E52D9ECB6805C81.quest_subtitle: "Gemstones from the Abyss"
	quest.5F55CD2D827BB910.quest_desc: [
		"Look, in all honesty I know you ate at least 3 of the previous white chalks considering your face is plastered in them."
		""
		"Just. Okay. Look. Yeah just, i mean it's calcium so at least you're getting some minerals...?"
		"So uh, yeah, uh, uhhhhh, this one surely doesn't taste- OHGODSTOP"
		""
		""
		"&b\"One must wonder what this vessel does, is it out of spite or is it for the love of absurdity\""
		""
		""
		"&7(You need this chalk to progress, use it for the upcoming rituals)"
	]
	quest.5F55CD2D827BB910.quest_subtitle: "Don't eat this one"
	quest.5FC9534817A442EA.quest_subtitle: "Making larger batteries"
	quest.601F4BCD183CC077.quest_desc: ["You'll need an Electric Blast Furnace to process this metal, if you haven't made one already. I'd recommend you do so."]
	quest.601F4BCD183CC077.quest_subtitle: "A mundane but durable metal"
	quest.60A1D50F6D8A1F40.quest_desc: [
		"Can be Hydrotreated for much higher lube outputs."
		""
		"Optioncally can be shoved in a vac freezer, lmao"
	]
	quest.60A1D50F6D8A1F40.quest_subtitle: "Lubricant Source"
	quest.62B2DFF0996CC216.quest_desc: [
		"Heat your Bauxite Solution then Centrifuge it, you'll get some red mud and a waste product."
		""
		"It is useful to recycle the waste product, but not required to *get* your titanium."
	]
	quest.62B2DFF0996CC216.quest_subtitle: "Titanium : Step 2"
	quest.634610E99CF32EB2.quest_desc: [
		"4k drives are what most players turn to early game for general storage."
		""
		"4k's are usually a sign your resource or crafting stockpiles can shoulder the extra circuit demand for these. If you struggle to make these it is worth considering what you are doing and process more things at once. "
		""
		""
		"No like seriously, how the hell did you get here without batch crafting. Seriously, craft stuff in like multiples of 16 to 64 or something unless it's brutally expensive lol"
	]
	quest.634610E99CF32EB2.quest_subtitle: "Earlygame bread and butter"
	quest.64F703DC26C9B9BF.quest_desc: [
		"No, do not, it's not grape flavored."
		""
		""
		"You'll need purple chalk to actually produce the pickaxe needed to mine Iesnium."
	]
	quest.64F703DC26C9B9BF.quest_subtitle: "Another chalk to the pile, is this old yet?"
	quest.6504044E7910A105.quest_desc: [
		"Any multiblock that accepts two+ energy hatches to boost recipe tier may also optionally just use a single 4A or 16A energy hatch."
		""
		"In short you need at least &e4 amps&r of power to boost the Recipe tier from one to the next"
		""
		"Eg. you need 4A LV to unlock a recipe Tier of MV (instead of LV)"
		""
		"Any power >&e4A&r will instead be routed to &bboost recipe speed&r rather than a 2nd Recipe Tier boost (In the case of 16A hatches)"
		""
		"Machines that accept only one energy hatch will never tier-boost with 4A or 16A hatches and will instead use the recipe tier of the hatch itself."
	]
	quest.6504044E7910A105.quest_subtitle: "How to run higher grade recipes."
	quest.6504044E7910A105.title: "Recipe Tier Boosting"
	quest.654F2B3B0CD1F42F.quest_subtitle: "Make a lot of this"
	quest.666A77BC58F33CD0.quest_desc: [
		"The Electric Blast furnace uses high heat and plenty of EU to smelt dusts into usable products."
		""
		"The EBF like many of the multiblocks you've made before has some new behaviors."
		""
		"Coil Temperature : Is a gate on what materials can be smelted alongside minimum EU. Coil temp is also gained from overclocks. "
		""
		""
		"Worth noting, any EBF recipe will gain a free overclock for every 2 coil tiers above the base tier listed. Example: A Cupronickel heat level recipe (1700K) will gain a free OC on an EBF with Nichrome Coils. "
		""
		"Standard Voltage Overclocks also apply."
		""
		""
		"Note about the quest itself : This is a deed quest, it will trigger a story sequence upon completing and viewing. Please wait for the cutscene to conclude fully!"
	]
	quest.666A77BC58F33CD0.quest_subtitle: "The First Big Furnace"
	quest.667FB6442C929BC0.quest_desc: [
		"This stuff comes from steam cracking Light Naphtha, which can be acquired by hydrotreating Sour Naphtha, or Cracked Naphtha."
		""
		"The key product is &aOlefin Gasses&r, this distills into several simple hydrocarbons you may frequently use."
		""
		"Funnily enough, you get more cracked Naphtha from this back, it's not a perfect conversion, you'll want to recycle this back to process out more materials."
	]
	quest.667FB6442C929BC0.quest_subtitle: "Light Naphtha"
	quest.66B6EFDC74821576.quest_desc: [
		"The Dimensional Mineshaft was mentioned in the Iesnium quests before. But here we are, you can now actually make this!"
		""
		"The dimensional mineshaft serves several purposes for resource collection early on."
		""
		"1. Iesnium creation, you want to avoid harvesting this from the nether as there's no good way to do so in bulk. "
		""
		"2. Malum Weeping Well products, Weeping wells are extremely scarce and quite frankly hidden in the depths of the world. To not waste your time more than I've already done, you can harvest them from the otherworld with specific catalysts."
		""
		"3. Runes, some ancient power has left behind some unknown language, don't think about it too hard."
	]
	quest.66B6EFDC74821576.quest_subtitle: "Getting More of It. Part 1."
	quest.66D9FFACAD1C761A.quest_desc: [
		"Somewhat, don't get too excited."
		""
		"&4Currently, Meteor Rituals are DISABLED, new Recipes will come somewhere before the 0.9 update"
		""
		"Neo vitae meteor rituals contain a host of common composite ores and some raw resources in ore form as well, allowing you to sidestep ore sorting and supplement resource demands directly."
		""
		"The drawback, they are rather annoying to harvest, ore extraction drills fill in meteors as stone so they don't clear the location. And Create drill walls fumble with any resource harder than Netherite."
		""
		""
		"There are several ways you may harvest them automatically, but they require a lot of extra effort which may not be justifiable for you."
		""
		"Create, AE2 Spatial Cube Slicing, Most likely other means of destroying blocks work as well."
	]
	quest.66D9FFACAD1C761A.quest_subtitle: "Renewable Ores*"
	quest.66D9FFACAD1C761A.title: "Neo Vitae Meteors"
	quest.66EAF78E0061AE13.quest_desc: [
		"For now your only source of primordial remnants is from harvesting it from outcrops in the lower layer of the firmament."
		""
		""
		"Once you can establish your own hardware within this dimension, you can automate this with new farming methods."
	]
	quest.66EAF78E0061AE13.quest_subtitle: "the hard part"
	quest.67110A5418804D33.quest_desc: [
		"You can't harvest pure nether quartz yourself, and gold is something only found in small amounts now."
		""
		""
		"I suggest you either raid bastions and trade with piglins, villagers, or consider getting to LV :^)"
	]
	quest.67110A5418804D33.quest_subtitle: "Piglin Economics 101"
	quest.677379DC62A11400.quest_desc: [
		"Tired of the summer and winter seasons!? Yeah me too! Make some glass, "
		"they'll make your crops &aimmune to the weather&r (as long as the glass is within &e16 bloocks&r AND can &esee the sky&r.)"
		""
		""
		"This seasonal immunity behavior also counts from crops below y-48 deep undervground."
		""
		""
		""
		"It's also pretty and glass is needed for progression, so you'll probably have spare glass for farms at some point :)"
	]
	quest.677379DC62A11400.quest_subtitle: "Making your crops stronger"
	quest.682E33E33C306E5E.quest_desc: [
		"Cooperite is your first proper source of Platinum and Palladium."
		""
		"This process is extremely lossy on Chlorine and other basic chemical precursors unti EV/IV where you can fully process all byproducts, so keep this in mind as you produce platinum."
		""
		"You can recover a decent amount, but some does get trapped in the insoluable plat metal dust."
		"(the large hexagon quest a little lower on this page)"
	]
	quest.682E33E33C306E5E.quest_subtitle: "Plat and Palladium Processing"
	quest.685F89265F6746A7.quest_desc: [
		"No get your mind out of the gutter. Stop."
		""
		"The atmosphere of various dimensions in frontiers are not naturally permissive to the idea of living. This is a fun way to say you'll &6suffocate&r in &acertain dimensions&r or &aat certain Y &alevels."
		""
		""
		"In the overworld, this is notably defined by around the &bdeepslate layer&r, going below this will trigger your characters &boxygen supply&r to start depleting"
		""
		"Speaking of, your oxygen supply is no longer 10 little bubbles on your hotbar. It is a full timer with a bar that visibly depeletes as you run out of air. You also naturally have &bmore air &bcapacity&r than normal."
		""
		""
		"There is also several ways to combat this hazard system."
		""
		"&eRebreathers&r, the simple rebreather will make you immune to low air environments like below the deeplsate layer. The Reinforced rebreather will make you immune to any environmental air hazard as long as you have a valid air supply, which can be Create backtanks or CosmicCore Bronze/Steel Supply Tanks."
		""
		"This system is also compatible with &ecreates diving helmet&r and will be once spacesuits are relevant."
	]
	quest.685F89265F6746A7.quest_subtitle: "Suffocation and you"
	quest.685F89265F6746A7.title: "Oxygen, Thin Air, Air Hazards"
	quest.687032030F774208.quest_desc: [
		"You basically have two options, either use a backtank or a steel air tank."
		""
		"you need a diving helment or advanced rebreather to use the steel air tank"
	]
	quest.687032030F774208.title: "Breathing in the Abyss"
	quest.688796D0E9E54832.quest_subtitle: "Early SMD Components"
	quest.69467329644E160D.quest_subtitle: "The inner casing"
	quest.6984F04E09CE50E5.quest_subtitle: "Chalk."
	quest.6C26FC61F619AAEE.quest_subtitle: "Almost there"
	quest.6CD224F26209A645.quest_desc: [
		"The harvest catalyst for Iesnium is, ironically, an Iesnium pickaxe."
		""
		"Do note, this pick will break, so make sure you have spare iesnium on hand to either repair the current one you have, or make new ones."
		""
		"You'll need a decent amount for LV+"
	]
	quest.6CD224F26209A645.quest_subtitle: "Actually getting more of it. Part 2."
	quest.6CE8034A84C58D0A.quest_desc: [
		"The Hemophagic transfuser allows you to mass automate blood magic materials with somewhat more ease."
		""
		"Attach Quintessentia hatches you your active vivariums and let them fill your anima network."
		""
		"Then use the hemophagic transfuser linked to imbument pylons to process materials en masse."
		""
		"It also can be upgrade to T4 to T6 altar by replacing the HV casings with EV or IV casings."
	]
	quest.6CE8034A84C58D0A.quest_subtitle: "The Sanguinmancers Mercy"
	quest.6CE8034A84C58D0A.title: "Tier 4 and beyond"
	quest.6E3EDA485D3AD5F7.quest_desc: [
		"In the waters of the undergarden you have discovered a strange, lightless chasm into the depths."
		""
		"The water rumbles as if it's alive and waiting for something."
		""
		"The topmost layer seeems to be mostly empty, with some landmasses poking up above what seems to be a thick fog."
		""
		"This fog threshold seems to be either holding something back, or keeping something out."
		""
		"Before Leaving, I heard some sort of clicking sound, aimed at me."
		"Something else is waiting for me down there."
	]
	quest.6E3EDA485D3AD5F7.quest_subtitle: "The only way forward, is down. (Y-64 to Y-200)"
	quest.6E3EDA485D3AD5F7.title: "The Hollow Abyss - Layer 1 : The Shaded Sea"
	quest.6E8CEE8F298636E8.quest_desc: ["While you can reach this, it doesn't have much uses yet, will be used later in MV, for now you can collect it and sort it if you want"]
	quest.6E8CEE8F298636E8.quest_subtitle: "WIP Content"
	quest.6E8D634B042DB26F.quest_desc: [
		""
		""
		"Across the hot and cold regions of this world seem to be plants that aid in thermal managment."
		""
		"Sun ferns spawn in &6hot biomes&r and help you with &bcold&r via &6heating coating&r"
		""
		"Ice ferns spawn in &bcold biomes&r and help you with &6heat&r via &bcooling coating&r"
		""
		"You can gain the combined benefit of both coatings by making &5Thermal Coating&r."
	]
	quest.6E8D634B042DB26F.quest_subtitle: "The Weather and You"
	quest.6E8D634B042DB26F.title: "Thermal Woes"
	quest.6ED6791358655950.quest_desc: ["Holds as much stuff as a double chest in one block, awesome!"]
	quest.6ED6791358655950.quest_subtitle: "Better Storage"
	quest.6EF94519E4BCBE72.quest_desc: ["Another Color to add to the pile, this time it's lime"]
	quest.6EF94519E4BCBE72.quest_subtitle: "Soooo"
	quest.6F0EB4BB758B4308.quest_desc: ["&o&7Ten feet twenty the flower man..."]
	quest.6F0EB4BB758B4308.quest_subtitle: "Lend me your power!"
	quest.6F15E6A210A0F091.quest_desc: [
		"Wood Tar can then be distilled into &eLight Tar Oils&r, &ePhenolic Oils&r, &6Creosote&r, and &cTar Pitch&r"
		""
		"Tar Oils and Phenolic Oils can be distilled once again for their final products, Creosote is just... Creosote, and Tar Pitch is still not implemented; so keep it stored around for now."
		""
		"I trust you can use EMI by now to see those products, if you somehow made it here without EMI..."
		"How? Better yet, why?"
	]
	quest.6F15E6A210A0F091.quest_subtitle: "Double Distillation Trouble"
	quest.6FEE469CCF433312.quest_desc: [
		"Can be produced from Gas Oils or Heavy Pyrolysis Oils."
		""
		""
		"The key product is &aOlefin Gasses&r, this distills into several simple hydrocarbons you may frequently use."
		""
		"This also gives you a variety of materials that can be recycled elsewhere."
	]
	quest.6FEE469CCF433312.quest_subtitle: "Gas Oils"
	quest.701373D09D99A565.quest_desc: [
		"Interfaces serve two purposes, as an input point for ME networks(by inserting items/fluids into them), or as extraction points for ME networks (by setting the filter and extracting the item/fluid that was filtered)."
		""
		""
		"This is much more efficient than using export/import busses, as the items are always immediately available. Import/export busses have their uses, but there's a good chance the interface may do it better."
	]
	quest.701373D09D99A565.quest_subtitle: "Interfacing with Interfaces"
	quest.70945C631B744AA2.quest_desc: [
		"Firebricks are strong enough to withstand the temperature and pressure of high pressure steam. As well as the hot temperatures required to smelt iron into steel. "
		""
		""
		"You'll want to make plenty of these, lets start with at least 1 stack."
	]
	quest.70945C631B744AA2.quest_subtitle: "More reliable brickwork"
	quest.70945C631B744AA2.title: "Firebricks"
	quest.70B26F634810EE5E.quest_desc: [
		"This will allow an MPS to run at HV Voltage."
		""
		"Upgrading all your current MPS's with these with give you a flat 4x'ing of your power generation and fuel usage. Useful for climbing into the next tier, but not enough."
		""
		"You Believe an even bigger engine is in store, soon..."
	]
	quest.70B26F634810EE5E.quest_subtitle: "Another MPS Upgrade"
	quest.70C78D038EBF6CA6.quest_desc: [
		"Rock Cutting wheels will cleave large areas of material away when active."
		""
		"Their SU cost scales with size. it's generally recommended to make many small blades vs 1 large one."
		""
		""
		"These are useful, strictly because you can automate mining with massive airships if you are so inclined. and attaching huge harvester arms to simulated contraptions for early game mining really changes how you play."
	]
	quest.70C78D038EBF6CA6.quest_subtitle: "Mass Contraption Mining"
	quest.71331803888BB83C.quest_subtitle: "The Endgoal"
	quest.7162A0976D025116.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Leyline compressor&r is one of the strongest multiblocks in the pack for strictly QOL functions."
		""
		"The &6Leyline compressor&r works by defining &epreconfigured structure patterns&r inside of the controller, this is the Pattern Encoding Page for Leyline Patterns."
		"Think of it like making an &bAE2 Crafting Pattern&r, but instead it's the &aexact layout of a multiblock&r."
		""
		"Once you have configured your multiblock as you desired, use \"&bValidate&r\" to double check it can even form to begin with, this is a requirement before you are allowed to \"&bEncode&r\" to avoid damaged/partial structure patterns."
		""
		"Once a pattern is encoded, place it inside of a &eME Leyline Hatch that is attached to a Leyline Compressor&r."
		""
		"&bRequesting that leyline package pattern from AE2&r will craft &nall blocks&r a structure needs, and then go a step further by compressing the block list into a '&6leyline package&r', this package may then be right clicked to place the &lentire structure&r at once in world. With a satisfying visual."
		""
		""
		"This is very useful for making common multiblocks easier to set up, it's up to you to figure out what works the best for your playstyle."
	]
	quest.7162A0976D025116.quest_subtitle: "Automatic Spatial Compression Rituals"
	quest.7171BE1689635624.quest_subtitle: "Your first source of Gallium"
	quest.71E1FB669BEB0D4C.quest_desc: [
		"Unlike Kanthal and other MV hot metals, HV+ Hot metals require the use of a Vacuum Freezer."
		""
		"If you haven't started working on EV circuits yet, return here once you have and also have assembled a Vacuum Freezer."
	]
	quest.71E1FB669BEB0D4C.quest_subtitle: "You'll need a vac freezer"
	quest.71E4C3FB3C4C06E9.quest_desc: [
		"Food is Frontiers is a &asoft-requirement&r system for progression."
		""
		"By default, you do not need food to heal, or food to stay alive, or infact use FTB Ultimine."
		""
		"The benefit of this is it removes the annoyance of having to eat food to stay topped up at home."
		""
		"However, to explore and survive other dimensions, you most likely will want some &eextra hearts&r, this is where food comes in to play."
		""
		""
		"Eating food applies &ball displayed values&r to the player, which is &6Bonus HP&r and &6Bonus &6Passive Regen&r."
		""
		"Any effects that &odo not show a timer beside them in brackets&r will last the &aentire meal&r &aduration&r. If there is a timer besides the effect, it will last as long as displayed."
		""
		"This turns food and meals into a &nbuffing tool for exploring&r, and some foods will be designed to aid you in these exploratory phases in Frontiers."
		""
		""
		"There is more to this system, like a taste pallet system for home eaten meals. But this is explained as you unlock and discover them through the QB.(And still in dev/testing partly) There's plenty of ways to augment your player through food while not having home feel annoying. And even some cool semi-permanent buffs you can apply to yourself."
	]
	quest.71E4C3FB3C4C06E9.quest_subtitle: "Custom Foods Inspired by Spice of Life Valheim."
	quest.71E4C3FB3C4C06E9.title: "Custom Meals and Hunger"
	quest.721AB809107498EB.quest_desc: ["Getting there, you've now mixed your materials into a ball of fireclay, you'll want to compress this into bricks before we create the proper block."]
	quest.721AB809107498EB.quest_subtitle: "ball of fireclay, or something"
	quest.72A429BEF13F8845.quest_desc: [
		"You can attune it to netherrack to scan for iesnium in the nether."
		""
		""
		""
		"If you have an AMD graphics card, you will need to modify the Occultism config file to enable AMD compatibility"
	]
	quest.72A429BEF13F8845.quest_subtitle: "Click Netherack"
	quest.73731AE01E78FE55.quest_desc: [
		"These blocks are vital to progression, I would not move forward into LV without making plenty."
		""
		"As such, you expect yourself to produce at least 8 of these machine hulls."
	]
	quest.73731AE01E78FE55.quest_subtitle: "The Core of a Machine"
	quest.73BC5E9DE8B0CE61.quest_desc: [
		"Some higher power notices your presence in the abyss and allows the natural magic of source to flow once again."
		""
		""
		"Spellbooks now function normally. Rather than failing to cast spells."
	]
	quest.73BC5E9DE8B0CE61.quest_subtitle: "Spellbook Release"
	quest.750F45A555ED46F1.quest_subtitle: "The start of coal chemistry"
	quest.75D7B3EAD5BAE28D.quest_desc: [
		"Look at the early LV Desalter. These blocks only exist for LV+MV tiers, but can help you produce earlygame liquid fuel that is more dense to transport around."
		""
		"Good power density, great for outputs, not too difficult to make and is renewable"
	]
	quest.75D7B3EAD5BAE28D.quest_subtitle: "Early Oil"
	quest.762D3321F43C0589.quest_desc: [
		"Last step! Take your &eChromium (III) Oxide&r and some &eAluminium&r and toss it into an &aEBF&r."
		"You'll get your &bChromium&r and some &bAlumina&r! Congrats, you've now (hopefully) automated Chromium"
	]
	quest.762D3321F43C0589.quest_subtitle: "Finally! Chrome!"
	quest.76CE8187246B0746.quest_desc: [
		"the first recovery process for this material makes you produce aluminium hydroxide."
		""
		"once you have a small batch of Aluminium Hydroxide, you can use it as a non-consumable to produce Sodium Hydroxide as a byproduct, rather than soda ask."
	]
	quest.76CE8187246B0746.quest_subtitle: "Even more hydroxide recovery"
	quest.7718E125AD134AA2.title: "Get Your Amine Back."
	quest.773E2ABCB902CA25.quest_desc: [
		"Reach the 4th layer of the abyss, Y:-700"
		""
		"The Ecological Dead Zone."
	]
	quest.773E2ABCB902CA25.quest_subtitle: "Abyss Layer 4: The Ecological Dead Zone"
	quest.773E2ABCB902CA25.title: "Reach the, bottom?"
	quest.77DABAF71C391FA3.quest_subtitle: "Robust Automation"
	quest.7886325B74847F55.quest_desc: [
		"Reaching the Firmament is a requirement to unlock major parts of HV. "
		"As such, you are required to make an initial expedition to the Firmament before you can grasp"
		"what is needed to proceed."
		""
		"Note: This dimension is currently under Functional Development, new features for Gravity Behavior and Content will show up in future Nightlies, but for now this quest and recipes to access the firmament are so you can check out what exists"
	]
	quest.7886325B74847F55.quest_subtitle: "The Skies Above"
	quest.78EEB9C6ED09C95E.quest_desc: [
		"I am so sorry for bucket hell."
		""
		"I'll clean this up eventually."
		""
		":')"
	]
	quest.78EEB9C6ED09C95E.quest_subtitle: "The start of wood refinements"
	quest.79797A9CA0D22B2A.quest_desc: [
		"Not Sure how I really want to 'integrate' or 'theme' ars into progression, Neo Vitae already feels alienated atm"
		""
		"Will most likely address that more in 0.9"
	]
	quest.79797A9CA0D22B2A.quest_subtitle: "A Dev Fiasco"
	quest.7A016FB22E827915.quest_desc: [
		"Diving below the heavy fog, the clicking seems to be more of a faint but persisting chittering."
		""
		"Something is moving through all of the water around me, some kind of &#9B3F9Dpathogen bloom&r, large dark masses of it float around."
		""
		"Off in the distance, I see a Gloomper Toad sink below the fog, out in the open water."
		""
		"In less than &#FF050A15 seconds&r the entire water turned into a chorus of clicking, chittering, and what I can only describe as a grotesque gurgling sound as the &#FF0505entire creature was dissolved whole&r."
		""
		"I will name this phenomena, \"&#D203E5The Murkbloom&r\", It is within my best interest that I stay as quiet, if not more quiet, as I would if dealing with a Warden."
		""
		"Something tells me I should &cavoid open water as often as possible&r, and listen to my surroundings &nvery closely&r"
		""
		"I tried to establish a warp point near the abyss, to find that this place is the source of &dAnti-magic emissions&r I've been dealing with. Seems Teleporting into the depths will be impossible for now."
		""
		"If I dive &cdeep enough&r, I might discover how to get my &aspell book&r working again."
	]
	quest.7A016FB22E827915.quest_subtitle: "Silence is the standard."
	quest.7A016FB22E827915.title: "An Unseen Threat: The Murkbloom"
	quest.7A0405D8C766C3C2.quest_desc: [
		"Worth noting: now that you have Nichrome coils, any recipe that only required Cupronickle coils will gain +1 free overclocks. "
		""
		"This is due to coil overclocking, to keep it simple, every +2 heat tiers above the base heat tier, you will gain +1 Free Overclocks. This can help massively speed up smelt times if maximized."
	]
	quest.7A0405D8C766C3C2.quest_subtitle: "Stronger heating. (3600k)"
	quest.7ABC4319FC83A545.quest_desc: [
		"The plantlife in the abyss has naturally adapted to not attracting huge murkbloom masses."
		""
		"Using these plants you can make a coating for your tools and armor. This coating will help reduce the disturbance caused to murkbloom. The higher the level the deeper the effect and potency is."
	]
	quest.7ABC4319FC83A545.quest_subtitle: "Hiding from Murkbloom "
	quest.7BAA63BF7EE181C3.quest_desc: [
		"Cuprosiva ore is one of the many Composite Ores that exist across the overworld."
		""
		""
		""
		"All Composite ore is truly 6 seperate ore types in one ore! you'll eventually learn to seperate the ore in increasingly complex sorting steps."
		""
		""
		"For now, you can directly smelt curposiva for copper."
		""
		"You can get &6Tin Dust&r by \"Manually Sorting\" Cuprosiva, hold right click on Crushed Cuprosiva to find some tin nuggets."
		""
		"Also worth noting, you can do this to Fersosine as well to get gold dust, same case for lead and silver"
	]
	quest.7BAA63BF7EE181C3.quest_subtitle: "Copper and Tin"
	quest.7BAF71B8957633BA.quest_desc: [
		"Gonna Be real with you, Neo Vitae is the Neoforge Version of BloodMagic and I've never used it"
		""
		"There are going to be some rough patches while I figure out everything."
		""
		"Have the guidebook on the house, you're gonna be reading it as much as I am to figure this out haha."
		""
		"&eOrbs are still the same, craft this thing, it's your knife as well as a crafting tool and you'll &eneed to use it to drain life essence from your player into the altar.&r"
	]
	quest.7BAF71B8957633BA.quest_subtitle: "Life shall be spilt"
	quest.7C2F955386C9378D.quest_desc: [
		"Congrats, if you got here, you've completed the pack up to the current available content!"
		""
		"Expand your base and bulk up your resource production, EV and higher will test the amount of power and infra you can assemble."
	]
	quest.7C2F955386C9378D.quest_subtitle: "END OF 0.8"
	quest.7C5DB25564510E87.quest_desc: [
		"Allows you to draw gray chalk runes, generally required for higher complexity ritual activations."
		""
		""
		"There's not much to say, another chalk to go into the pile."
	]
	quest.7C5DB25564510E87.quest_subtitle: "the base of better chalks"
	quest.7DC3441B47B3E2E8.quest_desc: [
		"HV multiblock hatches means access to EV power tier recipes, and upgrading speeds of anything you've been running so far"
		""
		"I would recommend you invest these into your EBF's"
	]
	quest.7DC3441B47B3E2E8.quest_subtitle: "Time to tier up again!"
	quest.7E41FC728C5BA186.quest_desc: [
		"This comes from &eRefinery Gas&r, which requires some special processing to desulphurize."
		""
		"I'd recommend you set up a passive &6Lean Amine Solution&r setup, somewhere in your processing line. And also take the time to clean any &6Rich Amine Solution&r you make."
		""
		"This one yields several other byproducts, including &eCracked Naphtha&r, which can be reprocessed into other materials as well."
		""
		"This recipe is one of the higher yields for &aOlefin Gasses&r."
	]
	quest.7E41FC728C5BA186.quest_subtitle: "Refinery Gas"
	quest.7ECF1D3CAA70ACD2.quest_desc: ["For future content, just store it for now."]
	quest.7ECF1D3CAA70ACD2.quest_subtitle: "NYI"
	quest.7F0D22395A2F8985.quest_desc: ["Worth noting you can farm this with the soul wood totem version of the unchained rite."]
	quest.7F43598A6495BC40.quest_subtitle: "Your First Coil"
	quest.7FE634D65F26BB7A.quest_desc: [
		"Bullet Peppers spawn throughout Crimson Forests or can be traded from Piglins!"
		""
		"You need to use a knife to harvest them."
		"Only the bottom block can be collected, rest will convert to sticks."
	]
	quest.7FE634D65F26BB7A.quest_subtitle: "Foods of the Nether"
